{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage","id":566515,"title":"Aggravated damage...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-24T09:08:16-07:00","id":566515,"title":"Aggravated damage...","content":"...and why werewolves can't inflict it? Seriously, I was really sueprised (and dissapointed) when I found no any gift which let Uratha to use it. The lack of this ability made them weaker than others I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:15:00-07:00","id":566556,"title":"","content":"...so why werewolfs can't inflict it? I was really disappointed when I've found no Facet or Gift which give the Uratha this ability. The lack of it made them weaker then others gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:18:11-07:00","id":566576,"title":"","content":"Eating a human or werewolf for essence turns your attack into aggravated damage. Mouth only.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're two honorary spirit ranks above a spirit, you do aggravated damage to said spirit. Honorary rank can be effectively increased via a rite.<br /> <br /> Using banes can do aggravated damage. Fire does aggravated damage to vampires, prometheans and mummies, there is a gift that gives fire Influence.<br /> <br /> Also, games aren't balanced against each other. Some are going have abilities others are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-24-2015, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:37:03-07:00","id":566592,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I find most abillities that allow you to deal aggravated damage to be intensely boring and mostly something aproriate for an antagonist.<br /> Bashing damage beats a foe. Lethal damage kills a foe. Aggravated damage <i>destroys</i> a foe. In most cases, you have a really hard time justifying why a person would stay and fight, after being dealt a few points of aggravated damage not to mention that it makes fights even shorter and more lethal than they already are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:38:49-07:00","id":566671,"title":"","content":"Aggravated Damage is the go to choice when you absolutely must destroy your opponent. It is terrifying and deadly, and it absolutely should be. Not something that you use at all times, to be sure, but is pulled out when you really, really need it. I find its lack of presence (as a Gift) disturbing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:42:42-07:00","id":566674,"title":"","content":"Why is aggravated damage not a gift? To make using silver something to actually consider. Why bother with a silver bullet if you've got agg claws?<br /> <br /> Seriously, I think its a question of wanting to make each Tribe have to work for their favored prey's bans/banes instead of having a single Gift act as a universal solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-24-2015, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:48:53-07:00","id":566683,"title":"","content":"Who said anything about Silver Claws/Jaws... I far prefer Savage Rending myself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Aggravated Damage is not a universal solution (at least it never was for us). It was a weapon of last resort. Most of our fights never needed that level of base damage. Lethal was often enough all that was necessary, but on rare occasions, when the stakes and odds were heavily stacked against us, and we just could not run for one reason or another, Aggravated Damage leveled the playing field. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:52:58-07:00","id":566685,"title":"","content":"There are several ways to access aggravated damage, including silver, exploiting Banes, cannibalism and a rite. That there is no easy switch-on aggravated-damage source amongst Gifts is very much an intentional and specific design choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:54:08-07:00","id":566689,"title":"","content":"Because Aggravated damage is a Werewolf's 'silver bullet', that carves through the otherwise incredible regenerative abilities, and is one of the only things capable of bringing down Gauru. Introducing such a power would be like giving a vampire the ability to shoot sunbeams from it's eyes.<br /> <br /> That said, Werewolves can access aggravated damage. There are several Fighting Styles that cap with an Agg dealer, and of course they can use silver. But weaker than other gamelines? Bad comparison. I don't see any other splats healing all bashing and lethal every single turn, or dishing out a reliable five to ten lethal damage on each swing. Nor do I see them dealing automatic tilts, lasting defense penalties, or crippling conditions at a moment's notice. Every splat is good at things within their themes, but it's best not to draw cut-and-dry comparisons between gamelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:55:53-07:00","id":566693,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but it's not a gift because it got promoted to a general werewolf ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:00:01-07:00","id":566696,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Duplicate threads merged.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:14:24-07:00","id":566707,"title":"","content":"Vampires have only one 'reliable' method of inflicting aggravated, and it requires you to have one Discipline at 4 dots and only works in frenzy. Good for those who have pledge to the Worthless One but otherwise sort of an expensive wild card. Beasts can inflict aggravated at the drop of a hat.<br /> <br /> Werewolves operate a bit of a middle ground, being inherently capable of it, but it's frowned upon, as well as being able to get it as an achievement with spirit rank, or using abilities to seek out banes and bans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:48:49-07:00","id":567035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=566707#post566707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires have only one 'reliable' method of inflicting aggravated, and it requires you to have one Discipline at 4 dots and only works in frenzy. Good for those who have pledge to the Worthless One but otherwise sort of an expensive wild card. Beasts can inflict aggravated at the drop of a hat.<br /> <br /> Werewolves operate a bit of a middle ground, being inherently capable of it, but it's frowned upon, as well as being able to get it as an achievement with spirit rank, or using abilities to seek out banes and bans.</div> </div> </div> </div> I still think, that without this ability werewolves will be in trouble in case of high-level fight, e.g. high-PU werewolf fight high-BP vampire. On this level, Gauru regeneration stop to be so big advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T14:51:56-07:00","id":567036,"title":"","content":"At that level they probably have enough ways to level the playing field.<br /> <br /> Fire spirit bound to a sword, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T15:02:36-07:00","id":567040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=567035#post567035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I still think, that without this ability werewolves will be in trouble in case of high-level fight, e.g. high-PU werewolf fight high-BP vampire. On this level, Gauru regeneration stop to be so big advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They might be. But the games aren't balanced against each other so that's entirely something that could happen.<br /> <br /> Alternatively your Storyteller might believe that vampires are still human and allow a werewolf to eat them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T15:22:53-07:00","id":567062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=567035#post567035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I still think, that without this ability werewolves will be in trouble in case of high-level fight, e.g. high-PU werewolf fight high-BP vampire. On this level, Gauru regeneration stop to be so big advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>At that point there are some many intervening factors, that even speculating is pointless. Just as an example: I've got two PC characters, both played by the same player but their a good fit. One is a Rahu combat monstrosity (remade from 1st ed), going at it he's got ~20 health, 25 dice worth of attack, 8 defense, between 1-3 armor and between a +9 or +10 weapon modifier with no initiative penalty. He can do quite a bit more, but that's the crux of it. The other character is a Ventrue duelist. He's rocking Light Weapons 5, Celerity 5, and a special artifact tool that treats itself as a universal bane to all things that suffer banes. 10 health, 12 dice of attack at +1 damage (aggravated), that jumps to 17 dice in Frenzy, 15 defense and two dots of Resilience.<br /> <br /> We were all bored, so at one point we played out the fight. The general finding being that, in the face of the Werewolf's insane attack pool and damage modifier the vampire could not possibly survive two successful attacks. Worse, against 3/3 armor he couldn't reliably deal more than two or three damage even on a successful attack, hardly enough to soldier through 20 health. Plus the Werewolf had Butchery so the vampire was only ever going to get one or two attacks before dual leg wrack spelled the end of his days. His only chance was employing Celerity interrupts to avoid attacks and feinting to reduce the Werewolf's defense, then to dump all his defense, Frenzy and stowed successes into one insane 40+ die hail mary attack. Which, even after two such assaults, was generally not enough to bring the Werewolf down (though he'd kick it the second he shifts down).<br /> <br /> And that's one example, between two characters without allies fighting head on. If the vampire was smart he'd just dominate a bunch of gun men to soften up the Werewolf, then ambush him with a rapier through the back of the head, or dominate the wolf himself for a convenient and extremely lethal lapdog. Countless combinations of allies, environments and circumstances render even this scenario pointless and inconclusive, to say nothing of all the other power combinations that could be at work. (Can the vampire turn into a cloud of killer mist? Can he become a locus of unholy fear and force the Werewolf to cower helplessly? Or can the Werewolf summon and control fire? Can he cripple the vampire and leave it helpless before the pack?)<br /> <br /> Basically, white rooms are pointless (well, not entirely, but for most of the time yes), and splats should not be compared, not least of all in a one vs one fight. The results rarely if ever translate into practical reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T21:36:03-07:00","id":567360,"title":"","content":"Fetishes are pretty insane, and with some prep a group of Werewolves can do some terrifying things.<br /> Not quite Mage level insane with prep, but still really frightening.<br /> And if they go out of their way to please the spirits and set them free soon afterwards, they can mitigate some of the political baggage of using so many fetishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T04:18:03-07:00","id":567632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=567035#post567035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I still think, that without this ability werewolves will be in trouble in case of high-level fight, e.g. high-PU werewolf fight high-BP vampire. On this level, Gauru regeneration stop to be so big advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why is it always a wolf v vamp fight? Why does no one ever care about a wolf v mage, or a wolf v changeling? I swear, its like cat people versus dog people. The cliche is that they're always fighting, but the animals themselves get along perfectly fine. Its the people that always try to say one or the other is better.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://sugarpoultry.deviantart.com/art/Werewolf-Vampire-Drama-180373780\" target=\"_blank\">http://sugarpoultry.deviantart.com/a...rama-180373780</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-25-2015, 07:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T05:03:49-07:00","id":567685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=567632#post567632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why is it always a wolf v vamp fight? Why does no one ever care about a wolf v mage, or a wolf v changeling? I swear, its like cat people versus dog people. The cliche is that they're always fighting, but the animals themselves get along perfectly fine. Its the people that always try to say one or the other is better.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://&quot;http://sugarpoultry.deviantart.com/art/Werewolf-Vampire-Drama-180373780&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">http://sugarpoultry.deviantart.com/a...rama-180373780</a></div> </div> </div> </div>1) Cuz VtR is the only gameline which is comparable with Forsaken and have 2.0 ed now. Demons and Beasts are too high level.<br /> 2) Cuz FurrvsFangs is famous stable trop.<br /> 3) Personaly, I don't like vamps - they arw arrognant and proud. So, if werewolves won't be strong enough they will be &quot;second-class&quot; as in any film, show or book when they live in one univers. Although, the last point is totally IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","user":"Lashet","date":". 06-25-2015, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:41:43-07:00","id":567919,"title":"","content":"Well, I will say this, from experience in our Werewolf Game.<br /> <br /> The Prince and several Vampires in our campaign were all capable of inflicting Aggravated Damage through their Disciplines. Generally Claws (which apparently still applies at Protean 4 in 2nd Edition yes? Someone made that statement anyways). The Werewolves were all pretty leery of them for this very reason. And rightfully so, in a few cases (specifically the Prince and his Council, whom we dealt with constantly). Additionally, many of the vampires, leery of the Werewolves also carried Silver to use against them. When our Pack started gaining power and influence, we became a threat to the Vampire community, to some extent, as we began &quot;interfering&quot; in their plans while we expanded our territory (there were of course several factions of vampires). When we managed to finally obtain Savage Rending, the odds shifted a bit. While we were always a physical threat to the vampiric community, they tended to regard us as something to just eliminate when the chance arose, and with Silver they were pretty good at it (and we, the PC's, were never stupid enough to just fight it out... werewolves are far better at the guerilla warfare game than vampires tend to be). Once we were able to deal direct aggravated (few werewolves carry flamethrowers around with them - though I will admit that our Irraka did carry magnesium flares with him at all times) this trend drastically changed.<br /> <br /> When we dusted the first vampire that tried to ambush one of us (2 of us had Savage Rending at that point), word got out. After a bit, they discovered that the Cahalith was no longer someone to trifle with (similar to Pendragon's example character above, he could throw high teen Dice (with a Fetish allowing him 8 Again) and had 22 Health Boxes towards the middle/end of the campaign) because he was capable of taking on pretty much all comers, and when the vampires DID try to gangbang him en masse, they discovered why he was the most feared Werewolf in the city. NONE of that would have happened had he not had Savage Rending (and Spirit Pack as well).<br /> <br /> Sometimes you need that threat of instant and immediate death that Aggravated Damage brings to the table. You don't need to resort to it all the time, of course (most of our fights remained non-aggravated throughout the campaign), but an armed society is a polite society as it were. Losing that core ability from 1st Edition (Savage Rending) for the ability to Eat for Aggravated was just a horrible choice, in my opinion. Yes, now anyone can do it essentially for free, but I feel that something very thematic was lost. No worries, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:43:42-07:00","id":567924,"title":"","content":"The thing is, short of some kind of arranged arena match, it's never going to be one werewolf versus one vampire. Werewolves hunt in packs. No werewolf would be stupid enough to go up against dangerous prey alone. Vampires tend to have lots of minions - ghouls, brainwashed humans, younger vampires trying to earn their favor, etc. and they almost never go into direct confrontation with their enemies. They pull strings and manipulate circumstances to remove their rivals without needing to get themselves involved. This whole one elder vampire versus one bodhisattva werewolf in a one on one caged match to the death is just such an artificial scenario, it doesn't actually exist outside of theory crafting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:05:18-07:00","id":567947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=567919#post567919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Prince and several Vampires in our campaign were all capable of inflicting Aggravated Damage through their Disciplines. Generally Claws (which apparently still applies at Protean 4 in 2nd Edition yes? Someone made that statement anyways).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in 2e, no; Protean weapons do not deal Aggravated by default. Accessing Aggravated damage in 2e for a vampire requires the vampire to <i>also</i> have a specific merit, iirc, <i>and</i> be in Frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:11:45-07:00","id":567950,"title":"","content":"When my 'low' power werewolf first encountered a vampire, the vampire turned invisible then stabbed him with some sort of cocktail of drugs and Vitae that knocked him senseless and gave him a mild Vinculum.<br /> <br /> But I think if he was planning on killing a vampire, he'd just wait till daytime and chomp their heads off while they slept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T09:02:23-07:00","id":568048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=567947#post567947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not in 2e, no; Protean weapons do not deal Aggravated by default. Accessing Aggravated damage in 2e for a vampire requires the vampire to <i>also</i> have a specific merit, iirc, <i>and</i> be in Frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which includes Riding the Wave of Frenzy, yes? Does not seem to be all that much of an issue to me. But I do get your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T14:45:34-07:00","id":568400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=568048#post568048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which includes Riding the Wave of Frenzy, yes? Does not seem to be all that much of an issue to me. But I do get your point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah. So... not only will they be more kill-minded, but they'll have a higher dice pool than they normally would...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T18:12:17-07:00","id":568564,"title":"","content":"Vampires can pretty much say bye-bye when the Hunter in Darkness finds their Haven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T04:48:33-07:00","id":569031,"title":"","content":"So, can werewolf with high-PU take down vampire with high-BP, abusing her own powers nor his weaknesses?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:06:28-07:00","id":569044,"title":"","content":"That's a silly qualifier.<br /> <br /> In the end, the answer is 'maybe,' and 'it depends.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:08:44-07:00","id":569045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=567685#post567685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Cuz VtR is the only gameline which is comparable with Forsaken and have 2.0 ed now. Demons and Beasts are too high level.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is simply not true. While we can argue that one gameline is &quot;more powerful&quot; than another (whatever that means), they never reach a point where one completely and utterly overpowers another. They all always remain competative with each other, and each gameline still remains the best at their individual focuses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2) Cuz Fur vs Fangs is famous stable trope. </div> </div> </div> I will conceed this point. It is famous, if rather annoying. However, I find it ironic that the reverse isn't true - few vampires care about a rivalry with werewolves. No one brings up about how badass a vampire needs to be compared to a were.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Personaly, I don't like vamps - they arw arrognant and proud. So, if werewolves won't be strong enough they will be &quot;second-class&quot; as in any film, show or book when they live in one univers. Although, the last point is totally IMO. </div> </div> </div> Anyone can be arrogant - that's an aspect of being human. The Ven might be, but that's the same with the Storm Lords and Silver Fangs. Awakened mages, on the other hand? That's the game's theme.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, look at Harry Potter or Dresden - second fiddle wolves, while vamps don't even exist. The simple fact of the matter is that, when a supernatural is the focus of the media (book, film, whatever), everyone else is second fiddle. This is even true in werewolf-focused novels - the wolves are dominant, and everyone else is second fiddle. Its just that werewolf stories are in the minority, compared to others, for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Vampires can pretty much say bye-bye when the Hunter in Darkness finds their Haven.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> The reverse is also true - a werewolf can pretty much say bye-bye when a Mehket finds their sleeping place. Using the Kiss on an unsuspecting sleeping target is as much of a death sentence as a silver bullet to the brain in this case. Lets be honest, attacking anyone while they're asleep is pretty much a win situation for the attacker.<br /> <br /> This is pretty much the problem with any crossover penis measuring contests. People either give one side advantages, the other side disadvantages, or they completely ignore the inherent limitations of the other supernatural's powers. Or they try to compare specific builds of one species to a generic stereotype minus all powers or merits of another. Ephsy's example falls apart when we start looking at low Blood Potency vampire - the damage is simply spread over too much time to affect any combat. Daytime no longer reduces their dice pools, and only deals damage if we're talking about direct exposure. Sneaking into a haven without windows is little different than sneaking into anyone's house while they're asleep.<br /> <br /> As well, it ignores bodyguards. While vampires aren't as pack oriented as werewolves, they are very much </span>subordinate <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">oriented - ghouls, revenants, and thralls are all very common. And, yes, that IS an advantage to being a vampire, as there's a reason there's so many covenant-based merits that grant access to such.<br /> <br /> <br /> Werewolves are the best at hunts, yes. In fact, I would likely say that a werewolf that managed to hunt down a vampire to their haven does have the advantage. Its their specialty. I would say the same thing about a werewolf hunting down a sleeping Beast to their Lair, or a demon to their Bolthole. Actually, hunting down a demon to the bolt hole would probably have already caused their Cover to shred massively, so they're likely already long gone with angels on their tail - the mere act of hunting them has effectively defeated them, or at least massively weakened them.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, in a direct fight, a werewolf in Garou actually has the advantage over a demon that Went Loud. Even with their high Premium, that demon doesn't have many options that can outdamage a raging werewolf's ability to heal all damage. And the demon is on a timer, with a Rank 5 hunter angel heading right for them after this particular stunt.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a direct fight between a Beast and Wolf has a number of potential outcomes, depending on the individual builds. There's no way to generalize this - while the werewolf has a number of innate abilities that directly apply to combat, the Beast has <i>none</i>. Its all Atavasms, Nightmares, Birthrights, and merits. If we're bringing in specific stuff for the Begotten, then we can bring in Fortified Form, Living Weapon, wolf fighting styles, fetishes, and Full Moon / Strength Gifts for the Uratha. The vast majority of combat powers of the Children still rely on spending Satiety as well if they intend on going up against another supernatural, and that's a far more precious resource than essence. Hells, the most effective combat Beast is already going to be low in the first place! I actually give advantage to the wolf here. They're naturally better at hunting and fighting, imho, and I feel that a specific werewolf build has more options than a specific Beast build. Which isn't that surprising. The Wolf Must Hunt. The Beast... must pick and choose new family.<br /> <br /> In a wolf v. vamp fight? Natural claws and fangs of the wolf already ignore the undead flesh*, reduce everything to bashing property of vampires, actually removing one of the strongest advantages vamps have in random fights. That, plus the frenzy ability, makes the best tactic for the vampire to be grappling and try to feed. They drink blood and heal, the wolf naturally heals, and they're in a stalemate without adding on powers. With powers, we start getting into things like Dominate v. Dominance, or Stealth+senses v. Obfuscate+Auspex, or using silver weapons against fire powers, and that just gets messy and overcomplicated, and pointless.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> * This particular ability is actually the main reason I'm particularly dismissive of the idea of agg-claws specifically for vampires. Wolves come with an anti-vamp ability built in. And all other prey already have weaknesses that the game wants you to focus on.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - I think I should also point out that vampires, werewolves, mummies, and prometheans are the only game lines where the PC supers are naturally violent / physical characters. Vamps have blood buffs and frenzy. Wolves have shapeshifting and death rages. Prommies were super-survivors with a lesser version of the blood buff. I only remember reading that freshly awakened mummies were insanely strong, I forget the details. Something to do with pillars?<br /> <br /> That said, mages don't have any physical powers that come naturally - they get mage sights and a mage armor, and the rest of the time they need time and preparation. Demons are natural spies and liars, but nothing says they'll ever have access to combat powers or forms. Its simple for the Begotten to never once have any physical powers. Changelings are awesome at pledges (wishes?), dreams, and illusions and making them real, but that's not the same thing as fighting prowress. Even Sin-Eaters, with their ghostly ability to survive death, had to invest in certain powers for offensive ability. Just as easily, we could have had oracles and necromancers that could only bleed plasm as they were chopped apart. Having defenses without combat ability to back it up does not make a splat adapt at physical things.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, given all the above, I really think that wolves are naturally very powerful compared to other splats during a crossover, let alone their natural enemies. There's already a large number of advantages against six of the ten lines in combat. The vamps already have to be wary of wolf claws. That leaves prommies and mummies, neither of which have a 2e conversion yet, and frankly are rare in the first place, making such crossover an exceedingly niche case. So, no. We don't need agg-claws because crossover. Hells, in the case of Sin-Eaters, there's no point to agg claws because of how bulwarks work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-26-2015, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:10:09-07:00","id":569046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569031#post569031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, can werewolf with high-PU take down vampire with high-BP, abusing her own powers nor his weaknesses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. And vice versa.<br /> My gut feeling is that one on one the vampire will win, Physical Intensity and Frenzy are stronger benefits than Gauru and suchlike (albeit only for high level vampires). In actual play though, the Werewolf will have a pack to back her up, whereas it's unlikely a vampire will have fellows on his level he can trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:33:44-07:00","id":569087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569046#post569046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yep. And vice versa.<br /> My gut feeling is that one on one the vampire will win, Physical Intensity and Frenzy are stronger benefits than Gauru and suchlike (albeit only for high level vampires). In actual play though, the Werewolf will have a pack to back her up, whereas it's unlikely a vampire will have fellows on his level he can trust.</div> </div> </div> </div> But... but... what about Gifts, Fetishes and Totem? May it help to werewolf ? Smt like Elemnts (pure), and Hit-and-Run and there was another good abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:36:47-07:00","id":569088,"title":"","content":"Sans Claws of the Unholy the vamp does have one glaring weakness: a finite fuel tank. You can only use physical intensity and healing so many times without a refill, whereas at high primal urge a werewolf will be able to shift to gauru and heal everything for free for a good few turns, and if they frenzy too they can keep it up even longer. And a vamp goes down at full lethal. A werewolf in gauru doesn't.<br /> <br /> So to take out a werewolf the vampire needs to completely fill their track with lethal multiple times, while a werewolf only needs to do it once, and can take as long as they like. And bear in mind a werewolf's natural weapons can easily be at +8 lethal damage with armor piercing at that level, even against vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:50:29-07:00","id":569107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569031#post569031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, can werewolf with high-PU take down vampire with high-BP, abusing her own powers nor his weaknesses?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pendragon posted an example combat between two highly combat-specced characters earlier in which the werewolf appeared to be the dominant force, so I'd suggest that the answer to this is 'yes'. Obviously that was under specific circumstances, but then context always triumphs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569087#post569087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But... but... what about Gifts, Fetishes and Totem? May it help to werewolf ? Smt like Elemnts (pure), and Hit-and-Run and there was another good abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, these things can all help a werewolf. The Purity Facet of the Gift of the Elementals is fully capable of scourging a vampire with a source of Aggravated damage once high level enough; other forms and Facets like Hit &amp; Run and the Urhan form power can let a werewolf evade an angry vampire just as a Celerity vampire can evade an angry werewolf; and so on and so forth. A Totem with Reaching and Blast can scoot around in Twilight while hammering a vampire that can't fight back.<br /> <br /> It's all swings and roundabouts. The werewolf has a tightly trusted pack; the vampire has less trusted but still powerful Kindred allies. The werewolf and the vampire both have mortal assets to lever; the vampire's probably possessing a wider swathe of mortal assets, while the werewolf has fewer but more loyal and also has spiritual assets to call upon. A vampire with the right build is <i>really</i> good at just mind-controlling things; a werewolf with the right build is <i>really</i> good at shrugging off mind-control attempts. Etc etc.<br /> <br /> When it comes to combat I would generally give the advantage to the werewolf; Gauru alone is a <i>huge</i> influence on how battles play out. However, both vampires and werewolves should play smart, fight dirty, draw on allies and generally do everything they can to stack the deck in their favour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T05:52:18-07:00","id":569108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569087#post569087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But... but... what about Gifts, Fetishes and Totem? May it help to werewolf ? Smt like Elemnts (pure), and Hit-and-Run and there was another good abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Of course they'd help. With a Crimson Falx you could lop off a vampire's arm, and with the urshul's Weaken the Prey gift you can give them Arm Wrack, rendering a vampire completely 'armless.<br /> <br /> Also a variety of other abilities. Tongue of Flame, Slaughterer, Barghest. Primal Strength, totems and fetishes of all sorts.<br /> <br /> Seidmadr may have been pointing out that during Frenzy a vampire gets to add their Blood Potency to all physical rolls, so they have a higher base damage dicepool. Along with their Physical Intensity, which lets them expend Vitae to add 2 to a physical dicepool of their choosing, making them capable of great feats of strength. It's actually sort of the opposite of gauru or Kuruth. Werewolves do get a large physical increase but the healing is more of a defensive mechanism that vampires don't have access to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-26-2015, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T06:00:25-07:00","id":569115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569087#post569087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But... but... what about Gifts, Fetishes and Totem? May it help to werewolf ? Smt like Elemnts (pure), and Hit-and-Run and there was another good abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, and Disciplines, Blood Sorcery or Mysteries of the Wyrm will help the Vampire. I was just talking about the basic template-benefits. From where to build the combat on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569108#post569108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Of course they'd help. With a Crimson Falx you could lop off a vampire's arm, and with the urshul's Weaken the Prey gift you can give them Arm Wrack, rendering a vampire completely 'armless.<br /> <br /> Also a variety of other abilities.<br /> <br /> Seidmadr may have been pointing out that during Frenzy a vampire gets to add their Blood Potency to all physical rolls, so they have a higher base damage dicepool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. You got that exactly right.<br /> To me it feels as if Frenzy has pretty much the same position as Gauru has; somewhat dangerous method of enhancing combat ability. It lacks the defensive bonuses (for all save Wyrm-Dragons, but that's another thing) of it, but it scales much better as an offensive thing. Same with Physical Intensity; when the Vitae/Turn begins to run away, this becomes an amazing power. But, like with Frenzy, it's mostly the Elders that can use this to great benefit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T06:07:26-07:00","id":569119,"title":"","content":"Vampires seem to be more explosive in their power than werewolves, who seem to focus on endurance and sustained buffs. Physical intensity gets insane at the top end, but at full blast you only get five shots at most. Make them count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T06:18:58-07:00","id":569124,"title":"","content":"Here is an appropriately core end-game build for a Rahu that is a total blender. I dread to think how much Experience this would require, but it's still fairly 'bare-bones' as I haven't drawn on Fighting Styles or a lot of other Facets that can boost it further.<br /> 5s in various appropriate attributes and skills, the appropriate specialty with Area of Expertise, etc.<br /> Glory 5 and Purity 5.<br /> Full dots in Living Weapon, Favoured Form and Fortified Form.<br /> The Berserker's Might and Slaughterer Facets from the Rage Gift.<br /> The Primal Strength Facet from the Strength Gift.<br /> The Shield-Breaker Facet from the Shaping Gift.<br /> Add enough Primal Urge to actually be able to activate enough things as required.<br /> <br /> This chap, in Gauru, has a base dice pool of 22 dice with 8-again, going to 25 with Willpower and 27 with All-Out Attack. He can roll the dice pool <i>twice</i> and choose the better result. On a hit, his claws deal 8L and have Armour Pierching 7, ignoring non-magical armour entirely. He has 19 Health levels, 10 Defence, Armour 2/2 and can reduce the damage from a single source per turn by 5 (or throw off a Tilt instead). If you're not his primary prey and are just <i>in his way</i> he's now got a base of 27 dice before WP and AOA. I'm probably missing some other easy sources of extra dice. Grappling him doesn't help because this is all natural weaponry &amp; Brawl in the first place.<br /> <br /> Then you get to active his final form with Crimson Spasm, and things get <i>really</i> stupid.<br /> <br /> Add Honour for, ex, Crushing Blow and Honed Rage, or Cunning for Unchained, and so on and so forth, and it gets even worse.<br /> <br /> I am really not concerned about werewolves not being killy enough <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T06:39:06-07:00","id":569147,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Full Moon Gifts can be really brutal. I'm really looking forward to second auspice gifts. I like the merits, too, though I probably won't dip into them for a while.<br /> <br /> Lots of things are going to be involved in fights, and an actual confrontation can probably be avoided through sneakiness. Vampires are asleep as long as the sun is in the sky. They can rouse to defend themselves but that's a distinct weakness on their part and something that can, and should, be taken advantage of.<br /> <br /> In the end it's going to depend a lot on your character, their abilities, how they use them, the surroundings, the opponent, and luck. I mentioned the car thing and the invisible thing, but my previous character was a changeling of the Autumn Court. He had an ability to know a person's fears, and little way to really use it to his advantage, as he lacked any intimidation and couldn't usually take advantage of said fears in a meaningful way. But just last session my werewolf used Know Thy Prey to find out an insulting nickname an NPC had when they were a kid and, presumably, was picked on for it. Using that in conjunction with his Hunter's Aspect and intimidation made them cry and run away. While in a Blood and Smoke game one vampire beat another, physically superior vampire just by frenzying, latching onto them, and drinking.<br /> <br /> Don't worry about the mechanics of it, or white room combat between two foes. Just have fun and enjoy the game. Whoever's 'stronger' stops mattering once you start having fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-26-2015, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T06:40:07-07:00","id":569151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569124#post569124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is an appropriately core end-game build for a Rahu that is a total blender. I dread to think how much Experience this would require, but it's still fairly 'bare-bones' as I haven't drawn on Fighting Styles or a lot of other Facets that can boost it further.<br /> 5s in various appropriate attributes and skills, the appropriate specialty with Area of Expertise, etc.<br /> Glory 5 and Purity 5.<br /> Full dots in Living Weapon, Favoured Form and Fortified Form.<br /> The Berserker's Might and Slaughterer Facets from the Rage Gift.<br /> The Primal Strength Facet from the Strength Gift.<br /> The Shield-Breaker Facet from the Shaping Gift.<br /> Add enough Primal Urge to actually be able to activate enough things as required.<br /> <br /> This chap, in Gauru, has a base dice pool of 22 dice with 8-again, going to 25 with Willpower and 27 with All-Out Attack. He can roll the dice pool <i>twice</i> and choose the better result. On a hit, his claws deal 8L and have Armour Pierching 7, ignoring non-magical armour entirely. He has 19 Health levels, 10 Defence, Armour 2/2 and can reduce the damage from a single source per turn by 5 (or throw off a Tilt instead). If you're not his primary prey and are just <i>in his way</i> he's now got a base of 27 dice before WP and AOA. I'm probably missing some other easy sources of extra dice. Grappling him doesn't help because this is all natural weaponry &amp; Brawl in the first place.<br /> <br /> Then you get to active his final form with Crimson Spasm, and things get <i>really</i> stupid.<br /> <br /> Add Honour for, ex, Crushing Blow and Honed Rage, or Cunning for Unchained, and so on and so forth, and it gets even worse.<br /> <br /> I am really not concerned about werewolves not being killy enough <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, I'm not either. Werewolves are killing machines. They just do it in a different way than Vampires, is all.<br /> <br /> Umm.. lessee... similar Vampire...<br /> <br /> 5's in Attributes and skills of course, same with specs and AoE's..<br /> Max out Celerity, Vigor and Resilience...<br /> I'm also assuming a Blood Potency of 5, because that's pretty end-game, but if it was higher, the stats would be, so capping it there.<br /> 17 dice attack pool, 21 with Vitae Expenditure, while still saving vitae for Vigor and Resilience. 26 with Frenzy, 29 with Willpower on that. 5L + successes on a successful bite attack. Not going All-Out because that's suicidal.<br /> 15 Health Levels &amp; 15 defence (Reduced to 10 against the Werewolf). Ordo Dracul can add 5 to each if they've gone Wyrm. And all can reduce incoming damage by 6.<br /> <br /> Could add stuff like Protean for better grappling dice pools or armour (and Agg Claws, while in Frenzy, if focused on that). A brawl-focused Professional Training would add 9-again to the attack, and transform those three WP dice to Rote Action, but that applies to both sides so it's not a mark in either side's favour.<br /> <br /> All in all. They look pretty similar, so I'm not that worried about one over-shining the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":585,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","user":"Seidmadr","date":". 06-26-2015, 09:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:08:24-07:00","id":569162,"title":"","content":"Oh, don't forget that gauru form also has a reduced penalty to hit due to defense. That could potentially swing a fight, depending on how skill reliant the target's not-get-hit pool is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:58:45-07:00","id":569206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569046#post569046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In actual play though, the Werewolf will have a pack to back her up, whereas it's unlikely a vampire will have fellows on his level he can trust.</div> </div> </div> </div> This is a gross misconception. Werewolves are all about the pack, yes. They get better synergetic abilities with the pack. However, vampires are all about subordinates. Ghouls, thralls, revenants, childer, lower status covenant allies. Wolves are less likely to have power struggles on the day to day, but when faced with outsiders, vampires are far from outnumbered. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569087#post569087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But... but... what about Gifts, Fetishes and Totem? May it help to werewolf ? Smt like Elemnts (pure), and Hit-and-Run and there was another good abilities.</div> </div> </div> </div> And when it comes to social manipulation, vamps have an edge. They both have significant advantages in various fields. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569088#post569088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sans Claws of the Unholy the vamp does have one glaring weakness: a finite fuel tank. You can only use physical intensity and healing so many times without a refill, whereas at high primal urge a werewolf will be able to shift to gauru and heal everything for free for a good few turns, and if they frenzy too they can keep it up even longer. And a vamp goes down at full lethal. A werewolf in gauru doesn't.<br /> <br /> So to take out a werewolf the vampire needs to completely fill their track with lethal multiple times, while a werewolf only needs to do it once, and can take as long as they like. And bear in mind a werewolf's natural weapons can easily be at +8 lethal damage with armor piercing at that level, even against vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div> How do you get +8 &quot;easily?&quot; I assume you mean automatic successes, as per weapons? That sounds like a rather specific combination of Gifts and merits to me.<br /> <br /> That said, claws of the unholy (or silver weapons) are aggravated damage. So, if you're going to bring those up, you have to bring up the fact that Gauru only heals bashing and lethal at the start of the turn. So, its not as easy as you suggest. Without that agg damage, you'd be right. But, if we're bringing in agg damage, we need to start talking about using fire on the vampires, which is where the situation goes down hill fast.<br /> <br /> If we don't? Then that's where the grappling-feeding tactic comes in. Its about the only way that the vamp can match a wolf in a long term battle that ignores powers, imho.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569107#post569107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it comes to combat I would generally give the advantage to the werewolf; Gauru alone is a <i>huge</i> influence on how battles play out. However, both vampires and werewolves should play smart, fight dirty, draw on allies and generally do everything they can to stack the deck in their favour.</div> </div> </div> </div> This. Werewolf is called the Physical game, and Gauru the &quot;killing form,&quot; for a reason. That said, its not like other games can't be competitive and win with tactics and creative players on their side.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569119#post569119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires seem to be more explosive in their power than werewolves, who seem to focus on endurance and sustained buffs. Physical intensity gets insane at the top end, but at full blast you only get five shots at most. Make them count.</div> </div> </div> </div> Naturally. Vampires are all about social violence and flying into dangerous rages at provocation. Werewolves are ultimately patient hunters, and Gauru is an extension of that concept. Each game has its specialties. Play into those specialties, that game wins. Play into another, the other game wins. <br /> <br /> Let the wolf hunt, the wolf wins. Play social manipulation and abuse, the vamp wins. Play academia, mage wins. Play spy, the demon wins. And so on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T09:32:00-07:00","id":569325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569124#post569124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is an appropriately core end-game build for a Rahu that is a total blender. I dread to think how much Experience this would require, but it's still fairly 'bare-bones' as I haven't drawn on Fighting Styles or a lot of other Facets that can boost it further.<br /> 5s in various appropriate attributes and skills, the appropriate specialty with Area of Expertise, etc.<br /> Glory 5 and Purity 5.<br /> Full dots in Living Weapon, Favoured Form and Fortified Form.<br /> The Berserker's Might and Slaughterer Facets from the Rage Gift.<br /> The Primal Strength Facet from the Strength Gift.<br /> The Shield-Breaker Facet from the Shaping Gift.<br /> Add enough Primal Urge to actually be able to activate enough things as required.<br /> <br /> This chap, in Gauru, has a base dice pool of 22 dice with 8-again, going to 25 with Willpower and 27 with All-Out Attack. He can roll the dice pool <i>twice</i> and choose the better result. On a hit, his claws deal 8L and have Armour Pierching 7, ignoring non-magical armour entirely. He has 19 Health levels, 10 Defence, Armour 2/2 and can reduce the damage from a single source per turn by 5 (or throw off a Tilt instead). If you're not his primary prey and are just <i>in his way</i> he's now got a base of 27 dice before WP and AOA. I'm probably missing some other easy sources of extra dice. Grappling him doesn't help because this is all natural weaponry &amp; Brawl in the first place.<br /> <br /> Then you get to active his final form with Crimson Spasm, and things get <i>really</i> stupid.<br /> <br /> Add Honour for, ex, Crushing Blow and Honed Rage, or Cunning for Unchained, and so on and so forth, and it gets even worse.<br /> <br /> I am really not concerned about werewolves not being killy enough <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569151#post569151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Oh, I'm not either. Werewolves are killing machines. They just do it in a different way than Vampires, is all.<br /> <br /> Umm.. lessee... similar Vampire...<br /> <br /> 5's in Attributes and skills of course, same with specs and AoE's..<br /> Max out Celerity, Vigor and Resilience...<br /> I'm also assuming a Blood Potency of 5, because that's pretty end-game, but if it was higher, the stats would be, so capping it there.<br /> 17 dice attack pool, 21 with Vitae Expenditure, while still saving vitae for Vigor and Resilience. 26 with Frenzy, 29 with Willpower on that. 5L + successes on a successful bite attack. Not going All-Out because that's suicidal.<br /> 15 Health Levels &amp; 15 defence (Reduced to 10 against the Werewolf). Ordo Dracul can add 5 to each if they've gone Wyrm. And all can reduce incoming damage by 6.<br /> <br /> Could add stuff like Protean for better grappling dice pools or armour (and Agg Claws, while in Frenzy, if focused on that). A brawl-focused Professional Training would add 9-again to the attack, and transform those three WP dice to Rote Action, but that applies to both sides so it's not a mark in either side's favour.<br /> <br /> All in all. They look pretty similar, so I'm not that worried about one over-shining the other.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So I ran some simulations for these two combatants(yeah I am this kind of person :P), here are some thoughts.<br /> <br /> Gauru's regeneration is the greatest game changer and if the vampire does not have a way to deal aggravated damage she will lose.<br /> The vampire dries out in just 3 rounds assuming it goes all-out on vitae after which it obviously loses. And she actually has no choice to do otherwise because she needs to activate resilience everyround or she dies in just two rounds(when she uses it she dies in 3), she needs to activate vigor every round or she has very little chance of stacking aggravated damage on the wolf. If the wolf does not all-out attack she needs to use celerity for surpise attacks to actually capitalise on her 27 dice(one less vitae for physical intensity). I am not assuming dodges with celerity because the wolf can use hit and run and... yeah.<br /> <br /> All in all frenzying without being able to inflict aggravated damage against a gauru specs werewolf is not going to work.<br /> <br /> Now if the vampire can inflict aggravated damage (assuming through +0dmg claws and the celerity for surpise attacks scenario), she more or less needs 2,2 rounds to kill the werewolf and will win if she gets the initiative and most often even if she goes second. If she does not use celerity this way and the wolf does not all-out attack again she will lose the fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 06-26-2015, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T09:47:42-07:00","id":569341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569325#post569325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So I ran some simulations for these two combatants(yeah I am this kind of person :P), here are some thoughts.<br /> <br /> Gauru's regeneration is the greatest game changer and if the vampire does not have a way to deal aggravated damage she will lose.<br /> The vampire dries out in just 3 rounds assuming it goes all-out on vitae after which it obviously loses. And she actually has no choice to do otherwise because she needs to activate resilience everyround or she dies in just two rounds(when she uses it she dies in 3), she needs to activate vigor every round or she has very little chance of stacking aggravated damage on the wolf. If the wolf does not all-out attack she needs to use celerity for surpise attacks to actually capitalise on her 27 dice(one less vitae for physical intensity). I am not assuming dodges with celerity because the wolf can use hit and run and... yeah.<br /> <br /> All in all frenzying without being able to inflict aggravated damage against a gauru specs werewolf is not going to work.<br /> <br /> Now if the vampire can inflict aggravated damage (assuming through +0dmg claws and the celerity for surpise attacks scenario), it more or less needs 2,2 rounds to kill the werewolf and will win if she gets the initiative and most often even if she goes second. If she does not use celerity this way and the wolf does not all-out attack again she will lose the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, as long as we're doing white rooms, could you run that again with the Werewolf having Hit and Run so he can interrupt the vampire's interrupts and trigger a Clash of Wills?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T09:58:06-07:00","id":569350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569341#post569341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, as long as we're doing white rooms, could you run that again with the Werewolf having Hit and Run so he can interrupt the vampire's interrupts and trigger a Clash of Wills?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do not tempt me, please!!! Although without the ability to inflict aggravated damage the result would be the same since the vampire always runs out of resources first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:07:36-07:00","id":569364,"title":"","content":"Haha fair enough. I think the whole scenario is a bit silly, because like I said a one-on-one fight between these characters with no outside factors will never actually happen short of a special WoD edition of Thunderdome.<br /> <br /> Two supernatural creatures enter! One supernatural creature leaves!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:12:39-07:00","id":569366,"title":"","content":"You can spend an Essence to instantly travel to the Hisil, or meatspace. Could you grapple an opponent and do that, bringing them there, then perhaps leaving them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:16:43-07:00","id":569370,"title":"","content":"I suspect that tactic would be heavily frowned upon. You're supposed to keep the shadow and material separate, not dump troublemakers in the spirit world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:29:55-07:00","id":569376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569366#post569366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can spend an Essence to instantly travel to the Hisil, or meatspace. Could you grapple an opponent and do that, bringing them there, then perhaps leaving them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Only in the area of a Locus, or with New Moon's Gift 5. But given one of those, yes, I imagine you could do that. I agree with Elfive to an extent, it would probably be seen as bad form to intentionally leave a creature of flesh stranded in the Shadow. And even with the lessened emphasis on the boarder patrol aspect in 2e, that doesn't seem like a very satisfying end to a hunt. I don't see &quot;out of sight, out of mind&quot; as something a werewolf would settle for when it comes to their prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:30:48-07:00","id":569378,"title":"","content":"Now, as the set up to an <i>ambush...</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:33:21-07:00","id":569381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569364#post569364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haha fair enough. I think the whole scenario is a bit silly, because like I said a one-on-one fight between these characters with no outside factors will never actually happen short of a special WoD edition of Thunderdome.<br /> <br /> Two supernatural creatures enter! One supernatural creature leaves!</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that rarely would a confrontation like this happen in an actual game but I need to know these things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> Also one last point, bad rolls are far more crippling for the vampire than the werewolf(because the vampire is on a 3 round timer both from the wolf's attacks and the draining of vitae) and they will cause the loss of the fight more often that not.<br /> So all in alI I'd say that a vampire, even the one in the second scenario should not be risking its eternal unlife in a clawfight with a rahu werewolf in gauru unless there is no other option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 06-26-2015, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:48:40-07:00","id":569407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569378#post569378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, as the set up to an <i>ambush...</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Or to separate prey from its allies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569381#post569381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So all in alI I'd say that a vampire, even the one in the second scenario should not be risking its eternal unlife in a clawfight with a rahu werewolf in gauru unless there is no other option.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to wonder, how does a vampire fare if they have a gun with silver bullets, say a 2 DMG one? Providing a werewolf didn't inflict Arm Wrack to get rid of it and the vampire has as many bullets as it needs, but no automatic fire.<br /> <br /> Or, alternatively, a +2 damage silver weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T10:52:36-07:00","id":569409,"title":"","content":"Against someone in gauru those are practically the same anyway. Your best bet is to be faster than the werewolf and stay out of claw range. <br /> <br /> So I think a vamp's best bet is to run backwards at celerity speed firing while the wolf chases them. Screaming in terror optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T11:04:48-07:00","id":569417,"title":"","content":"The main difference is that with a melee weapon, Vigor factors into the matter. With a ranged weapon, the gauru does get the benefit of bullet dodging, but the vampire doesn't get a discipline to amplify their dexterity, just physical intensity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T11:20:02-07:00","id":569447,"title":"","content":"If we're talking about silver bullets then having to hit more times while outside melee range seems preferable to having to hit less whilst within it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T11:26:11-07:00","id":569449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569417#post569417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main difference is that with a melee weapon, Vigor factors into the matter. With a ranged weapon, the gauru does get the benefit of bullet dodging, but the vampire doesn't get a discipline to amplify their dexterity, just physical intensity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. In this scenario the vampire is attacking with just 11 dice(assuming 5+1+5) versus the 10 defence of the rahu. To deal any meaningful damage the vampire will need to use physical intensity and celerity to keep away and make surprise attacks but this once again puts in on a timer of less than 5 rounds. On the other hand the rahu can use the damage reduction glory facet (depending on what facets she has activated her essense pool would be arround 12) and might not even need to stay in gauru until she actually catches up with the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T11:38:36-07:00","id":569456,"title":"","content":"In this scenario the vampire doesn't want to be using Celerity. She wants Obfuscate 3 to rob the Werewolf of it's ability to sense her. Celerity helps no doubt, but as others have said the timer is too short to deal the damage she needs. Protean 4, for wings, could also work, though one good jump from the Werewolf and the tides are turned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T11:58:58-07:00","id":569470,"title":"","content":"I could see Obfuscate screwing with most werewolves, it certainly worked on mine. But especially if a fight's already occurred there's blood tracking, and afterwards Impossible Spoor might require a Clash of Wills but pretty much specifically searches for the only things vampires leave behind as traces.<br /> <br /> With Obfuscation 3, 'He leaves no scent and makes no sound, though his passing leaves incidental signs, like drifting smoke or creaking floorboards.'<br /> <br /> With Impossible Spoor, 'The lingering photons disturbed by the prey's shadow; the slowly settling ripple of air currents disturbed by the prey; the electromagnetic handshake of the prey's smartphone with a wireless hotspot - all leave a trail this werewolf can follow.'<br /> <br /> I think the whole werewolf/vampire thing should be played up more in-world. Not necessarily as enemies, like in old World of Darkness but something. Especially since they're both territorial hunters often operating on the same territory. I'm hoping the Forsaken by Rome dark era shows some of their attitudes towards the dominant vampires of Rome, though I know it's focusing more on the barbarian nations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T12:05:11-07:00","id":569474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569364#post569364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Haha fair enough. I think the whole scenario is a bit silly, because like I said a one-on-one fight between these characters with no outside factors will never actually happen short of a special WoD edition of Thunderdome.<br /> <br /> Two supernatural creatures enter! One supernatural creature leaves!</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually... *cough* I kinda have one of those in my crossover games... its a competition between warriors in three person teams, highly popular among the supernatural population as a kind of sport that's one part battlefield, one part game of ball. Like quidditch with swords instead of flying brooms. Competition between fans is highly fierce, complete with rioting and bar room brawls.<br /> <br /> Its a running joke that all the fang v. fur stories came from some people watching two of the teams fight off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T12:08:48-07:00","id":569479,"title":"","content":"Indeed, I'd say its a good sign for crossover that both splats have measures and countermeasures that puts the other on edge. Vampires and Werewolves antagonize one another well, no in the one vs one white room sense (though they appear to do well enough there), but in the sense that they cover much the same ground but in very different ways. Both use methods the other would look at as disgusting, if not outright taboo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T12:18:21-07:00","id":569485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569206#post569206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is a gross misconception. Werewolves are all about the pack, yes. They get better synergetic abilities with the pack. However, vampires are all about subordinates. Ghouls, thralls, revenants, childer, lower status covenant allies. Wolves are less likely to have power struggles on the day to day, but when faced with outsiders, vampires are far from outnumbered.<br /> <br /> And when it comes to social manipulation, vamps have an edge. They both have significant advantages in various fields.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I was more of the impresison that a pack tends to be more on the same level than a vampire family. Vampires are more likely to be one old one dominating a lot of younger ones. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569325#post569325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So I ran some simulations for these two combatants(yeah I am this kind of person :P), here are some thoughts.<br /> <br /> Gauru's regeneration is the greatest game changer and if the vampire does not have a way to deal aggravated damage she will lose.<br /> The vampire dries out in just 3 rounds assuming it goes all-out on vitae after which it obviously loses. And she actually has no choice to do otherwise because she needs to activate resilience everyround or she dies in just two rounds(when she uses it she dies in 3), she needs to activate vigor every round or she has very little chance of stacking aggravated damage on the wolf. If the wolf does not all-out attack she needs to use celerity for surpise attacks to actually capitalise on her 27 dice(one less vitae for physical intensity). I am not assuming dodges with celerity because the wolf can use hit and run and... yeah.<br /> <br /> All in all frenzying without being able to inflict aggravated damage against a gauru specs werewolf is not going to work.<br /> <br /> Now if the vampire can inflict aggravated damage (assuming through +0dmg claws and the celerity for surpise attacks scenario), she more or less needs 2,2 rounds to kill the werewolf and will win if she gets the initiative and most often even if she goes second. If she does not use celerity this way and the wolf does not all-out attack again she will lose the fight.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, really? I thought the vampire would be dealing enough roll-over damage from the lethal teeth that at least some of it would stick! <br /> But yeah. Even with the stolen blood with the bite attacks, going back 4 Vitae/turn is going to bleed the vampire dry very fast (pun intended). <br /> <br /> Say, what does your simulations say would happen if both would have a Brawl-focused Professional Training maxed out, so they both use Rote Action on their attacks instead of +3 attack dice?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T13:11:09-07:00","id":569521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569474#post569474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Actually... *cough* I kinda have one of those in my crossover games... its a competition between warriors in three person teams, highly popular among the supernatural population as a kind of sport that's one part battlefield, one part game of ball. Like quidditch with swords instead of flying brooms. Competition between fans is highly fierce, complete with rioting and bar room brawls.<br /> <br /> Its a running joke that all the fang v. fur stories came from some people watching two of the teams fight off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's freaking awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T14:15:18-07:00","id":569572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569485#post569485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I was more of the impresison that a pack tends to be more on the same level than a vampire family. Vampires are more likely to be one old one dominating a lot of younger ones.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ah, really? I thought the vampire would be dealing enough roll-over damage from the lethal teeth that at least some of it would stick!<br /> But yeah. Even with the stolen blood with the bite attacks, going back 4 Vitae/turn is going to bleed the vampire dry very fast (pun intended).<br /> <br /> Say, what does your simulations say would happen if both would have a Brawl-focused Professional Training maxed out, so they both use Rote Action on their attacks instead of +3 attack dice?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah using the teeth solves the problem of drying out in three turns, but the fact still remains that the average number of rounds that the werewolf needs to kill is three with little variation due to the huge 9 or 10 minimum damage per attack it gets, so it is close to impossible for the vampire to stack enough damage to kill the werewolf before it dies. Also this is the second fact I mentioned, which is that bad rolls affect the vampire more that the wolf.<br /> <br /> I am not on my computer right now so I cannot run this but my guess would that the first scenario more or less remains the same since even if we assume that the Rote quality will increase efficiency by 100%(which it doesnt, mainly what it does is make sure your rolls are at least average) the vampire still needs way more than 3 rounds to kill while the werewolf would kill at the second or at the worst third hit practically everytime.<br /> <br /> On the other scenario the vampire would get close to the guaranteed two-shot winning the duel if she wins the initiative and would depend on what the rahu does on his own turns if she went second.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also the vampire <b><i>needs</i></b> to surpise attack the werewolf or the scenarios get much worse for our fanged duelist, more or less bringing it down to three rounds in the second scenario(with no rotes).<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Another interesting fact, which is directly related to the original topic of the thread, is that while werewolves cannot deal aggravated damage with attacks unless the storyteller permits the bite for essence thing to work on vampires, it has no effect on the duel since the vampire cannot afford to spent vitae to regenerate, if it did would actually decrease it chances of winning.<br /> <br /> Another note: English is not my first language so excuse me if I do not make sense sometimes.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 06-26-2015, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T15:26:27-07:00","id":569698,"title":"","content":"Couldn't the vampire just kite the werewolf till gaoru runs out?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T15:42:21-07:00","id":569705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569698#post569698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't the vampire just kite the werewolf till gaoru runs out?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It could, it could also get a dozen ghouls to shred the werewolf with autofire, or the werewolf could run to the nearest locci and jump to the shadow or assault the vampire with mass create fire and a trillion other scenarios BUT we are white rooming here and in this particular white room excercise we wanted to find out if a combat specced vampire riding the wave could stand against a gauru specced rahu at power stat 5 and with all relevant powers maxed out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T15:52:45-07:00","id":569711,"title":"","content":"Well, note that we haven't been actually using the other thing the Purity 5 Rahu has access to - Crimson Spasm.<br /> <br /> On average dice rolls, that can give the Rahu an additional 10 Strength, Dexterity or Stamina, or 5 Armour or additional levels of Lethal on her natural weaponry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T15:53:40-07:00","id":569712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569705#post569705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It could, it could also get a dozen ghouls to shred the werewolf with autofire, or the werewolf could run to the nearest locci and jump to the shadow or assault the vampire with mass create fire and a trillion other scenarios BUT we are white rooming here and in this particular white room excercise we wanted to find out if a combat specced vampire riding the wave could stand against a gauru specced rahu at power stat 5 and with all relevant powers maxed out. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Even in a white room scenario movement and tactics are allowed. I mean you've mentioned surprise attacks which is more than just sitting there wailing on each other and that relies of more things than playing keep away does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:01:47-07:00","id":569714,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, the best combat Vampires have in their arsenal is probably Primeval Misama. Turn into a cloud of bloodsmoke for as long as you damn well please, total invulnerability to everything that isn't sunlight, fire, a character specific bane or with storyteller approval: very heavy winds (and of course Pattern assaults, but that's the wrong gameline). Vampire forces her way into the Werewolf's lungs and chokes him to death while sucking Vitae directly from his Bloodstream.<br /> <br /> Combine that with Obfuscate and you're a blood mist no one can see. Or add in Nightmare and become a bloodmist the victim is too terrified of to fight back. Perhaps Celerity to reflexively turn into a bloodmist with attacked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 06-26-2015, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:06:26-07:00","id":569717,"title":"","content":"At Primal Urge 5, death rage lasts 30 minutes. You better have a big white room.<br /> <br /> There's this great book, <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Gun-Machine-Warren-Ellis-ebook/dp/B007ZFIMC6/\" target=\"_blank\">Gun Machine</a>. It's like Werewolf meets God Machine. I don't normally make associations to World of Darkness while I read but it was very 'the wolf must hunt,' despite the fact that there was no actual werewolf, it was while we were getting spoilers and I kept thinking Iron Master, or Predator King co-opted by God Machine. I bring it up because werewolves can use guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:11:11-07:00","id":569721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569714#post569714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, the best combat Vampires have in their arsenal is probably Primeval Misama. Turn into a cloud of bloodsmoke for as long as you damn well please, total invulnerability to everything that isn't sunlight, fire, a character specific bane or with storyteller approval: very heavy winds (and of course Pattern assaults, but that's the wrong gameline). Vampire forces her way into the Werewolf's lungs and chokes him to death while sucking Vitae directly from his Bloodstream.<br /> <br /> Combine that with Obfuscate and you're a blood mist no one can see. Or add in Nightmare and become a bloodmist the victim is too terrified of to fight back. Perhaps Celerity to reflexively turn into a bloodmist with attacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot how nuts that was. So yeah, it seems like a Protean, Vigor, Strength based brawler would be pretty insane.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569717#post569717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At Primal Urge 5, death rage lasts 30 minutes. You better have a big white room.<br /> <br /> There's this great book, <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/Gun-Machine-Warren-Ellis-ebook/dp/B007ZFIMC6/\" target=\"_blank\">Gun Machine</a>. It's like Werewolf meets God Machine. I don't normally make associations to World of Darkness while I read but it was very 'the wolf must hunt,' despite the fact that there was no actual werewolf, it was while we were getting spoilers and I kept thinking Iron Master, or Predator King co-opted by God Machine. I bring it up because werewolves can use guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time is actually pretty irrelevant actually. What matters is the size, and white rooms, at least in any forums I've used discussed them in, are assumed to be like the room of spirit and time from DBZ, a flat floor, stretching out infinitely in every direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 06-26-2015, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:16:47-07:00","id":569744,"title":"","content":"Hopefully the Brothers of Ypres will get a nice upgrade too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:18:19-07:00","id":569765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569712#post569712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in a white room scenario movement and tactics are allowed. I mean you've mentioned surprise attacks which is more than just sitting there wailing on each other and that relies of more things than playing keep away does.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True but you need to take into account that the werewolf can choose to go into death rage after the duration ends(which at this level of primal urge is like half an hour) so the vampire will run out of vitae for celerity long before that and she needs10 vitae for two rounds of peak performance which only wins in the best case scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569714#post569714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, the best combat Vampires have in their arsenal is probably Primeval Misama. Turn into a cloud of bloodsmoke for as long as you damn well please, total invulnerability to everything that isn't sunlight, fire, a character specific bane or with storyteller approval: very heavy winds (and of course Pattern assaults, but that's the wrong gameline). Vampire forces her way into the Werewolf's lungs and chokes him to death while sucking Vitae directly from his Bloodstream.<br /> <br /> Combine that with Obfuscate and you're a blood mist no one can see. Or add in Nightmare and become a bloodmist the victim is too terrified of to fight back. Perhaps Celerity to reflexively turn into a bloodmist with attacked.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work but it takes us too far out of the scernario, like I said before in an actual confrontation there are way too many options that could turn the fight one way or the other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 06-26-2015, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T16:21:04-07:00","id":569771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569721#post569721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I forgot how nuts that was. So yeah, it seems like a Protean, Vigor, Strength based brawler would be pretty insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's see: Strength 5, Brawl 5 (Grappling), Vigor 5, Protean 5 for Primeval Misma. There we've got a vampire with 16 dice in a Grapple, more with Physical Intensity. Lets add Nightmare 1 so the Werewolf can't spend willpower and the Vampire can reflexively harass him and his buddies with minor illusions (like a constant, low, maniacal cackling or perhaps glimpses of the vampire within the miasma). Illusions will be especially important if the vampire needs to corral her victim somewhere away from light and fire.<br /> <br /> In this form the vampire can keep the strangle offensive up, well, pretty much as long as she wants. Thirty minutes of death rage might get boring, but with a constant drip of Vitae and her prey chasing phantoms it's really just a matter of waiting till the furry bastard passes out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569765#post569765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could work but it takes us too far out of the scernario, like I said before in an actual confrontation there are way too many options that could turn the fight one way or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sticking strictly to fisticuffs (or fisticlaws as the case may be) I cannot see a Vampire coming out on top, especially against that Rahu, without a source of aggravated damage <b>and </b>a means to avoid harm for several turns. Take, for instance, the most aggressive possible vampire (in terms of dice). Physicals at 5 across the board, Protean 4, Vigor 5, Coil of the Wyrm 5, Riding the Wave Style 5, Blood Potency 5. That right there is a vampire with 24 dice of attack at +2 Lethal Damage assuming she spends willpower every turn. If the Werewolf forgoes his defense every action the vampire will average somewhere between 6 - 10 successes each turn, which is still (even with +7 lethal) not enough to conquer the Rahu's 19 fucking health.<br /> <br /> Conversely the Werewolf needs to touch the vampire maybe three or four times for that +8 weapon bonus to do the job. Worse, jacking the Vampire's defense up as high as it can go (Celerity 5, Wyrm 5, BP 5), we cap at 15. 20 if the storyteller rules that this vampire is definitely not disadvantaged by Gauru. Which leaves the Gauru with between 4 &amp; 10 dice to hit.<br /> <br /> Going with the best case scenario for the vampire, where she voids the Werewolf's attack five times in a row and proceeds to Resilience soak every subsequent hit, the odds are still not exactly in her favor as she may be contending with high armor (even after armor piercing 2 drops it), good defense and Gauru level healing. The fight isn't unwinable for the vampire, nor easy for the Rahu, but if I had to place my money I'd put it on the wolf.<br /> <br /> A reminder of the Rahu I'm comparing it to:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Here is an appropriately core end-game build for a Rahu that is a total blender. I dread to think how much Experience this would require, but it's still fairly 'bare-bones' as I haven't drawn on Fighting Styles or a lot of other Facets that can boost it further.<br /> 5s in various appropriate attributes and skills, the appropriate specialty with Area of Expertise, etc.<br /> Glory 5 and Purity 5.<br /> Full dots in Living Weapon, Favoured Form and Fortified Form.<br /> The Berserker's Might and Slaughterer Facets from the Rage Gift.<br /> The Primal Strength Facet from the Strength Gift.<br /> The Shield-Breaker Facet from the Shaping Gift.<br /> Add enough Primal Urge to actually be able to activate enough things as required.<br /> <br /> This chap, in Gauru, has a base dice pool of 22 dice with 8-again, going to 25 with Willpower and 27 with All-Out Attack. He can roll the dice pool twice and choose the better result. On a hit, his claws deal 8L and have Armour Pierching 7, ignoring non-magical armour entirely. He has 19 Health levels, 10 Defence, Armour 2/2 and can reduce the damage from a single source per turn by 5 (or throw off a Tilt instead). If you're not his primary prey and are just in his way he's now got a base of 27 dice before WP and AOA. I'm probably missing some other easy sources of extra dice. Grappling him doesn't help because this is all natural weaponry &amp; Brawl in the first place.<br /> <br /> Then you get to active his final form with Crimson Spasm, and things get really stupid.<br /> <br /> Add Honour for, ex, Crushing Blow and Honed Rage, or Cunning for Unchained, and so on and so forth, and it gets even worse.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Edit: </b>A bit of math and rolling later... Vamp doesn't stand a chance. He needs to be rolling somewhere in the realm of 18 successes, Eighteen! To deal the Werewolf a single point of lasting damage past the Werewolf's regeneration and damage reduction. Best dice pool I could muster was 30, saving a Vitae for Vigor and another to dodge, which gives him pool odds. <br /> <br /> On the flip side, give him a silver butter-knife or claws of the unholy and the fight flops to the other side. The vampire spits out 10+ aggravated damage per turn for five turns while being functionally untouchable. It's not totally undoable for Rahu, if he rolls well on Crimson Spasm and picks up four or more points of armor he may be able to tank his way to victory. Even so he's got to go a solid 8 rounds staring down 13-14 dice of +5 Aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 06-26-2015, 08:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T17:40:25-07:00","id":569808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569771#post569771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Edit: </b>A bit of math and rolling later... Vamp doesn't stand a chance. He needs to be rolling somewhere in the realm of 18 successes, Eighteen! To deal the Werewolf a single point of lasting damage past the Werewolf's regeneration and damage reduction. Best dice pool I could muster was 30, saving a Vitae for Vigor and another to dodge, which gives him pool odds.<br /> <br /> On the flip side, give him a silver butter-knife or claws of the unholy and the fight flops to the other side. The vampire spits out 10+ aggravated damage per turn for five turns while being functionally untouchable. It's not totally undoable for Rahu, if he rolls well on Crimson Spasm and picks up four or more points of armor he may be able to tank his way to victory. Even so he's got to go a solid 8 rounds staring down 13-14 dice of +5 Aggravated damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is really late here and I am still not on my computer so take this with a grain of salt.<br /> Assuming we are using the previous vampire character, he can only keep this up for 3 rounds. Expending one vitae for vigor, one for celerity and three for amplification, plus riding the wave to get to the 29 dice of attack. If he holds his move action to dodge with celerity he loses the benefit of surprise attacks which means that he rolls 19 dice, average 7 successes for 12 damage(7 after reduction) so he needs 3 attacks to kill the wolf. If he does not manage to pull that of the next round he is on zero vitae(zero vitae means no resilience so even the OHKO is possible, no vigor so no 5 automatic damage and minus 6 dice on attacks, this leads to 13 dice and requires a minimum of 6 successes to even inflict damage). That is without the possible health levels from crimson spasm which add at least another round, something the vampire cannot afford.<br /> <b>Most importantly</b> though we are now using the dodge with celerity option which I opted to omit from my tests because the wolf can also dodge with hit and run, and if she does she can practically starve out the vampire of vitae without a scratch on her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 06-26-2015, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T01:19:26-07:00","id":570030,"title":"","content":"I think there's an important non-crossover reason for restricting Werewolves access to agg. If Werewolves had easy access to agg why would they ever care about learning a spirit's bane? Easy access to agg takes a major piece away from Forsaken, hence why it's gone in 2e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T02:58:45-07:00","id":570086,"title":"","content":"Very interesting thread this! I like it!<br /> <br /> I've been thinking a bit, and looking about, and it looks like the biggest advantage Vampires have is weapons; for some reason the damage-enhancing werewolf gift only works with Brawl attacks, not with weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T03:37:38-07:00","id":570109,"title":"","content":"Because it's not really enhancing the attack, it's enhancing the teeth/claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T04:07:39-07:00","id":570115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=570109#post570109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's not really enhancing the attack, it's enhancing the teeth/claws.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know, but that doesn't make me like it any more. It forces fighter-Uratha to go unarmed, because it is simply so much better than armed combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T04:20:48-07:00","id":570138,"title":"","content":"Yeah... I think that might be the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T04:47:49-07:00","id":570156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=570115#post570115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, but that doesn't make me like it any more. It forces fighter-Uratha to go unarmed, because it is simply so much better than armed combat.</div> </div> </div> </div> Ummm.... we're talking about werewolves, right? Isn't going in with just claw and bite a classic image? Why wouldn't you want that? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T06:42:24-07:00","id":570224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=570086#post570086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">for some reason the damage-enhancing werewolf gift only works with Brawl attacks, not with weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>By default, sure, but you could easily just make a Fetish weapon that worked with it if you wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T10:03:41-07:00","id":570318,"title":"","content":"Yes. The book is heavy on the Strength + Brawl front. But that makes sense, since that's the core of werewolf and it is the new core book. I expect some expansions will expand more, for instance if we get detail on the Lodge of the Gargoyle perhaps a Gift or line of fetish rifles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T10:20:54-07:00","id":570326,"title":"","content":"I could also see lodge of the shield being big on handguns, batons, and tazers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T10:28:11-07:00","id":570327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=569698#post569698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Couldn't the vampire just kite the werewolf till gaoru runs out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not if he Kuruths, and then he gets half his facets to use for free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T10:30:45-07:00","id":570329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=570156#post570156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ummm.... we're talking about werewolves, right? Isn't going in with just claw and bite a classic image? Why wouldn't you want that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because it's boring. It locks down choice. If one wants to be an effective combatant, you have to go Brawl. <br /> <br /> I'm just a bit sad that one has absolutely 0 reason to do cool stuff like tear down a lamp post and smash some guy with... because you'll do more damage just ripping him up with claws. <br /> I suppose I'd have liked it a bit more if that facet had been more like how the Vigor discipline works. Enhancing strength-based attacks in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T15:07:22-07:00","id":570624,"title":"","content":"I'm glad we don't have werewolves ripping up lamp posts to use as weapons, that's superhero imagery and this isn't a superhero game. That's Apocalypse territory, and since I have both games I'm glad they are differentiated enough to feel like different games. It's only locking down choice if you are trying to min/max the system, there's nothing preventing you from making less mechanically optimal choices in favor of stylistic choices (and as an ST I'd find a way to reward that player as that's the kind of person I prefer to game with.)<br /> <br /> Diablo 3 comes to mind. My &quot;shotgun horses&quot; build is more efficient at dealing damage but my &quot;army of archers&quot; build looks cooler and is just more fun to play and I get more enjoyment out of the less efficient build. Same applies here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T22:07:21-07:00","id":570966,"title":"","content":"Depending on how Lodges turn out in 2e this could have a benefit to one particular group. The Claws of Ashes rite used by the Lodge of Scars was nifty in principle but mechanically seemed odd since it just gave you &quot;aggravated +2&quot; damage when using your claws. In hindsight I'm not sure if it meant it turned your claws into 2A weapons or if it gave a flat +2 on top of agg or if it did agg and then 2 automatic bonus damage, but yeah.<br /> <br /> At any rate the final example of stuff 5-dot fetishes can do in 2e is &quot;to count themselves as the bane of something that doesn\u2019t usually suffer a bane.&quot; Which seems like a roundabout way of saying &quot;does agg to a thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> If your ST is exceedingly generous they might let you create a Tooth of the Death Wolf. Not to be confused with a Tooth of the Death Wolf though, completely different fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2079-red-9","name":"Red 9","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2079_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T22:23:42-07:00","id":571010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=570329#post570329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Because it's boring. It locks down choice. If one wants to be an effective combatant, you have to go Brawl.<br /> <br /> I'm just a bit sad that one has absolutely 0 reason to do cool stuff like tear down a lamp post and smash some guy with... because you'll do more damage just ripping him up with claws.<br /> I suppose I'd have liked it a bit more if that facet had been more like how the Vigor discipline works. Enhancing strength-based attacks in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Purity Facet of the Gift of Strength does exactly that.<br /> <br /> There is plenty of reason to use weapons - maybe you're in a situation where you need to stay in Hishu form. Maybe you have a Fetish weapon that has some advantage over teeth and claws. Maybe you need a particular weapon for a Spirit's Bane, or a silver weapon to fight other werewolves. Heck, maybe you just have a weapon with more than a +2 modifier and you don't have the Slaughterer Facet. Not every character is going to have Slaughterer. Not even every combat character is going to have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T22:23:48-07:00","id":571011,"title":"","content":"Who needs lamp posts when the world has been blessed by the great god <a href=\"http://www.eldritchdark.com/writings/short-stories/88/the-great-god-awto\" target=\"_blank\">Awto</a>.<br /> <br /> Somewhere there's a werewolf who's mastered a variant of Beast Talker that allows them to converse with machines. And they've got a fetish that's amplified their Command Artifice facet. And they roam around their territory with a pack of cars, running down prey with awakened automobiles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T03:01:02-07:00","id":571106,"title":"","content":"Weaponry use has plenty going for it already - fighting styles, fetish weapons, bane material construction, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T08:33:08-07:00","id":571430,"title":"","content":"Killer Instinct works with weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T09:18:17-07:00","id":571500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=570329#post570329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's boring. It locks down choice. If one wants to be an effective combatant, you have to go Brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, it doesn't lock down choice. You can make fetish swords and guns. Nothing stops you from being a silver bullet sniper, or specializing in knife fighting with Dalu. There are plenty of effective choices. And even then, you're confusing what effective means. Effective combatant just means you're competent, not a combat god. And the most effective way of a combatant? Banes and bans. Everyone has a weakness, and specializing in that weakness is the best way to go. Silver, rituals to increase your spirit rank, Claimed exorcisms, fire.<br /> <br /> What I think you mean is &quot;if one wants to be a combat munchkin,&quot; which is an entirely different matter. No one is forcing you to buy all these Gifts with the limited amount of XP you earn- there are other areas you can invest in, such as Fighting Styles, Professional Training with a Firearms or Weaponry skill focus, defensive tactics, or being all assassin-backstabby. Or, horror of horrors, spread your experience out among other fields instead of a laser focus on combat ability.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. Attacking with fang and claws is classic. When most people think &quot;werewolf attacks,&quot; they're thinking of using power of the wolf to attack with. Wolves aren't exactly renowned for opposable thumbs and using tools, they're famous for shapeshifting. So, naturally, that style is going to have a lot of attention over the others. <br /> <br /> But you still have access to all the mortal abilities and merits, and there are a large number of merits and Gifts that work with any werewolf form, plus fetishes. There are plenty of viable options.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just a bit sad that one has absolutely 0 reason to do cool stuff like tear down a lamp post and smash some guy with... because you'll do more damage just ripping him up with claws.<br /> I suppose I'd have liked it a bit more if that facet had been more like how the Vigor discipline works. Enhancing strength-based attacks in general. </div> </div> </div> You can already do both. Plus? Werewolves aren't vampires - why would you want to act like one? Vampires have their areas of expertise, wolves have theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 06-28-2015, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T17:11:32-07:00","id":572017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=571500#post571500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I think you mean is &quot;if one wants to be a combat munchkin,&quot; which is an entirely different matter. No one is forcing you to buy all these Gifts with the limited amount of XP you earn- there are other areas you can invest in, such as Fighting Styles, Professional Training with a Firearms or Weaponry skill focus, defensive tactics, or being all assassin-backstabby. Or, horror of horrors, spread your experience out among other fields instead of a laser focus on combat ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually. I was thinking kind of the opposite. Brawl already have many things going for them, including the versatility, and the fact that you don't need equipment for it. A facet like Slaughterer makes it a way to become a good combatant with much less focus. Allowing characters to be effective fighters without a laser focus on combat ability.<br /> <br /> And.. It's not exactly about munchkining. It's more... I need reasons why an Elder Uratha should carry weapons now. A veteran of decades of horribly close combat is going to end up fighting in the best way possible, and right now that is Brawl.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/585-seidmadr","name":"Seidmadr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar585_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T17:19:48-07:00","id":572018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=572017#post572017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And.. It's not exactly about munchkining. It's more... I need reasons why an Elder Uratha should carry weapons now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending on how much stuff from 1e's take on werewolf culture carries forward* I feel as though &quot;I am literally swinging around the legendary vessel of a god&quot; bears a sizeable impact on one's legacy, to say nothing of how one Facet of a Gift with tribal proprietary affinity isn't exactly the purview of every elder to begin with or how Touchstones are a little easier for creatures that are half incarnate symbolism to keep hold of when they have a manifest reminder of their humanity like a physical tool.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* And given that Only One Way To Win was included in the Fiction Anthology I suspect that &quot;werewolf culture cares about renown even beyond the death of the subject&quot; hasn't gone away.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T19:59:06-07:00","id":572114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seidmadr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=572017#post572017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually. I was thinking kind of the opposite. Brawl already have many things going for them, including the versatility, and the fact that you don't need equipment for it. A facet like Slaughterer makes it a way to become a good combatant with much less focus. Allowing characters to be effective fighters without a laser focus on combat ability.<br /> <br /> And.. It's not exactly about munchkining. It's more... I need reasons why an Elder Uratha should carry weapons now. A veteran of decades of horribly close combat is going to end up fighting in the best way possible, and right now that is Brawl.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know what you mean. But I don't think you have to worry. The core book was mostly about the core of werewolves, of the Forsaken. They had to hold back a lot on a lot of fronts, like the Pure and Hosts and the best tribe, the Ninth Tribe. I don't think that means they meant to not support them as much as they wanted to focus on the foundation of being a werewolf, which is tooth and claw.<br /> <br /> Even then, we have the Lodge of the Gargoyle and like Charlaquin said the Lodge of the Shield, both of whom are probably pretty skilled when it comes to firearms and are likely not without some firearms and weaponry-based gifts and fetishes prominent among their lodges. And in the fetish section we have the Crimson Falx, which is a Decapitated Condition and a snicker-snack away from being a vorpal blade.<br /> <br /> All that said, the first edition book placed the emphasis mostly on tooth and claw too, with just three sample klaives in the book and gifts that worked to enhance the natural weaponry of werewolves more than external ones, and we didn't get things like moon klaives and the gazhdum and arrathudum for about a dozen books in. Though we did get the Lodge of Arms pretty soon, I thought they could have been way cooler with everything that's been done with intelligent weapons. Anyways, we got an in-touch developer and cool writers, I'm sure we'll get more than enough reasons for werewolves to use weaponry and firearms in future books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-28-2015, 11:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T22:14:30-07:00","id":579467,"title":"","content":"Didn't vampires suffer from drinking werewolf blood in 1e? Like you needed a specific merit or bloodline or something to be able to stomach vitae derived from werewolves. That's my memory, at least. No idea if this followed over to 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> Also, I realize the werewolf vs. vamp portion of this thread is sort of passed, but this just occurred to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T22:30:57-07:00","id":579477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=579467#post579467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't vampires suffer from drinking werewolf blood in 1e? [\u2026] No idea if this followed over to 2nd Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>No and no. Werewolf Vitae was potent but unstable in 1e, giving you more fuel out of the deal but penalizing your frenzy rolls in the process. No word yet on whether this has carried through, though Acrozatarim suspects supernatural Vitae carrying weird tradeoffs is no longer a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T10:41:38-07:00","id":579971,"title":"","content":"I think they need a merit now to draw sustenance from supernatural creatures' blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T11:02:53-07:00","id":579983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=579971#post579971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they need a merit now to draw sustenance from supernatural creatures' blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The Merit was written pretty ambiguously, but the intent is that it's supposed to make the blood of other supernatural creatures count as vampire blood for the purposes of Blood Potency-based feeding restrictions. Without the Merit, werewolf (and other supers) blood functions just like human blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T13:32:10-07:00","id":580123,"title":"","content":"I'd say the <i>living </i>supernaturals count as regular humans without it. If you want to drink a mummy you'll need the merit regardless of your blood potency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T15:07:50-07:00","id":580281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=580123#post580123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the <i>living </i>supernaturals count as regular humans without it. If you want to drink a mummy you'll need the merit regardless of your blood potency.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. If the vessel doesn't have actual Blood, you'll need Unnatural Affinity to get Vitae from them at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T16:53:00-07:00","id":580343,"title":"","content":"Would of course add damage to a vampires bite. If a vampire wins a grapple roll, and gets an exceptional sux, they can damage and feed - the latter of which does up to BP in damage, to humans at least. Now - if the vampire loses a few grapple turns, he can't stand up to gauru; if he does win a few times, however, the steady flow of blood pumped back into pushing the grapple - could get messy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/668-hoodedclaw","name":"hoodedclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T01:47:22-07:00","id":580662,"title":"","content":"He's basically got to hold on until gauru times out. Since any werewolf with a vampire latched onto them like that would be sensible to just let kuruth take them when their control time expired, this could take between ten minutes and twelve hours. <br /> <br /> Practice on a mechanical bull might help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T07:16:41-07:00","id":580920,"title":"","content":"Or riding the wave with blood buffing to stay on. But, really, I think we've far and away entered the territory of the absurd. Even if we could perfectly achieve a stalemate here somehow, and the werewolf was willing to allow Kuruth that could kill innocent bystanders... and we're somehow not bringing Gifts, Disciplines, banes, or anything else into play...<br /> <br /> I mean, in theory, we could start talking about trying to feed the raging wolf vitae - sacfice a hand to bleed into its mouth. There's no longer a time limit between drinks, so a vamp could feed enough to fully blood bond the wolf, which leads to other complications... And a number of people still feel that feeding from a wolf should use the 1e rules of 2.5 vitae and -2 frenzy (as Condition?)<br /> <br /> And then, there's the Scarred Condition from biting we need to consider, and, while a Gauru can heal, its debatable if we can choke someone in Gauru out... Well, lets just say that this isn't going to be a simple comparison ever. Too much to think about even if we just compare innate traits, and not Clan/Cov/Tribe/Auspice, powers, or racial merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-06-2015, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:24:43-07:00","id":584609,"title":"","content":"Oh-key. So, there isn't the only answer.<br /> I just don't know, should I like werewolves. 2.0. Their corebook is pretty solid for me, but... I can put up with they are weaker than Demons, Beasts and Mages (cuz this three spluts is elite of WoD-verse) and if they will be weaker than Mummy or Promethean, or even Geists and Changellings. But if they are weaker then vamps, for it make them misfits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:34:15-07:00","id":584620,"title":"","content":"Weaker, how exactly? In a fight? Werewolves are meat-grinders with legs and fur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:50:57-07:00","id":584651,"title":"","content":"Plus with stuff like the Gift of Elements and Weather werewolves can equal Mummies in the &quot;town killing&quot; department. Seriously, I don't want to be on the same continent if a Protectorate ever goes to war with a Nome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:52:04-07:00","id":584652,"title":"","content":"Against some vamp-puppies. But if old strong vampire can easy take down the werewolf of the same lvl, it means that vampires are more advanced creatures than werewolves, accordingly...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:54:36-07:00","id":584653,"title":"","content":"Well, they can't so that's not an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T07:27:58-07:00","id":584723,"title":"","content":"Weaker? Hardly, dear. 2e werewolves are scary as hell. I feel that a combat-based werewolf is probably stronger than a combat-based demon, vampire, or beast. <br /> <br /> Vampires, in a fight, are good for going powerful in the short term before losing strength. If they can't kill the wolf off quickly in a fight, they lose. Vampires are best at using controls, either of the mind or grapples variety. If they can't do either of those to the wolf, they really don't stand a chance, imho.<br /> <br /> Demons have the small issue of needing to be human-like or fiery angels of doom coming to kill them, and Going Loud for Primium 10 isn't as powerful in direct combat as you'd think - sure, a handful more dice on some stuff, but is it enough to put down someone that has natural armor and regenerates Size+Stamina+3+Purity health in a single turn? Not helpful, and a stalemate favors the wolf - killer angel on the way, remember. If you want to take down a werewolf as a demon? You need to play the assassin or sniper card. Get somewhere safe, pull out a gun, take the time to Hellfire it and boost its power, and shoot. Direct combat is BAD for the Unchained. <br /> <br /> Beasts, despite people's OMG! reaction to the Atavisms, aren't actually that powerful until they get really high Lair. As far as I've been able to tell, most people are still looking at Beasts through the lens of 1e. There's a lot of scary feeling to them, sure, but a lot of it isn't really applicable to a fight. Being scary is absolutely a theme of Beast: the Primordial - being a killer is not. And all that is assuming a combat-built character; a social character wouldn't be able to fight back at all in combat. <br /> <br /> We haven't seen 2e mages in full yet, so we have no idea on their combat potential. Assuming they'll be walking gods again when the magic system is being changed around is premature. No clue on how anyone else handles it either, so assuming someone or another is going to be better is premature.<br /> <br /> The regeneration in an all out brawl against one of the wolves is insane. This makes the werewolves virtually unstoppable unless we're talking about using silver, or some form of aggravated damage. And, yes, that above is all white room crafting. I know, I know, its not really worth mentioning, because its unrealistic inside the actual game, and context matters. But here's the thing. Context is important because it allows people on one side or another to play to their strengths. <br /> <br /> Vampires can control you. Demons can sneak up on you. Beasts can terrify you. Werewolves? They hunt you down. They're not combat machines. They're killers. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, lets step away from combat for a minute. How are wolves outside of combat? Surprisingly good. They are, hands down, the best trackers in the game. There's even a Gift for tracking someone by the photons disturbed by the shadow they cast! How cool is that? Basic shapeshifting Gifts let them appear as anyone else. There's a lot of dominance-style social manuevering. You might not be the world's best diplomat, but you are definitely good at getting the results you need. In terms of raw magic? Access to spirit allies is not something to shrug off.<br /> <br /> Honestly, Werewolf is a pretty awesome game. I would never put them as weak.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T07:40:15-07:00","id":584727,"title":"","content":"Ah, yes, Skin Thief. AKA &quot;Did that blood thrall just punt an Elder through the wall?&quot; in the right hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:13:20-07:00","id":584750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=584652#post584652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Against some vamp-puppies. But if old strong vampire can easy take down the werewolf of the same lvl, it means that vampires are more advanced creatures than werewolves, accordingly...</div> </div> </div> </div> What makes you think old, strong vampires can take down a werewolf of the same &quot;level?&quot; Also, what do you mean by level?<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. A high Blood Potency vampire can arguably spend more vitae a turn, and frenzy for more bonus dice. Eventually (in theory) they'll have enough dice that they can hit the werewolf with enough damage in one turn to kill them, even in Gauru.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, a werewolf at character creation can use Efficient Killer to deal an amount of damage equal to their full dice pool as automatic successes to a vampire if they can lower the vamp's defense to 0. And there's lots of ways to do that - a powerful wolf would surely have them.<br /> <br /> In terms of rocket tag, the werewolf wins.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And all this is outside of context. A far more likely scenario is that the elder is going to get greedy and do his best to try and mind control and/or blood bond the wolf's pack so he's got a supernatural herd - its hard feeding when you're an elder. Meanwhile, a wolf isn't going to challenge a vampire to a duel at sunset in an empty room - they'll come hunting through the shadows, or the Shadow, and aim for an ambush. <br /> <br /> The wolf will have his pack. The vamp will have his ghouls, revenants, thralls, and misc vampire subordinates. <br /> <br /> The amount of situations we can bring up is staggering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-09-2015, 11:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:26:08-07:00","id":584762,"title":"","content":"May be. I just have some issues. IMO, durarion of Gauru could be longer (e.g. Willpower+PU). Or Crushing Blow - this facet could have another effect and let werewolf to inflict aggrav. damage, while she in Gauru form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:29:28-07:00","id":584768,"title":"","content":"Gauru might not even enter into it. Do you know how many ways an elder werewolf potentially has of setting something on fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:38:52-07:00","id":584776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=584762#post584762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May be. I just have some issues. IMO, durarion of Gauru could be longer (e.g. Willpower+PU). Or Crushing Blow - this facet could have another effect and let werewolf to inflict aggrav. damage, while she in Gauru form.</div> </div> </div> </div> You do realize that, if you don't mind Kuruth, Gauru can last until you run out of things to kill? And, since we're talking about a high PU character... that's going to be a while before you need to worry about time expiring.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:40:09-07:00","id":584779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=584762#post584762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May be. I just have some issues. IMO, durarion of Gauru could be longer (e.g. Willpower+PU). Or Crushing Blow - this facet could have another effect and let werewolf to inflict aggrav. damage, while she in Gauru form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, there is no time limit to Gauru form, as long as you're ok with potentially causing some collateral damage. And aggravated damage is much more rare in 2nd edition than it was in 1st. The fact that werewolves can deal agg to humans, wolves, and other werewolves at-will for no cost other than the social consequences of swallowing the meat (and potentially a Breaking Point towards Spirit, though that could be a good thing depending on your Harmony) is already pretty bonkers for 2e. Add to that automatic agg to spirits 2 or more ranks lower than them, and the fact that werewolf teeth are considered supernatural weapons in all forms (therefore ignoring resistances to mundane weapons, like vampire damage reduction) and honestly, werewolves really push the boundaries as far as damage types go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:04:29-07:00","id":584984,"title":"","content":"The book is already out in completion. There may be later books that add thousands of aggravated damage merits, but until then you've been given ample reasons and explanations for how your concern that vampires will always win against werewolves, and thus are 'second class' is unwarranted.<br /> <br /> If you want a merit, or another facet, just make one.<br /> <br /> First Class (\u2022)<br /> Prerequisite: Werewolf<br /> Effect: When in the general vicinity of a vampire, a werewolf always does aggravated damage to anyone they attack. On an exceptional success while attacking a vampire, targets with Blood Potency lower than the werewolf's Primal Urge are instantly vaporized.<br /> Drawback: To take advantage of the power the merit offers, werewolves have been known to go into battle with vampires strapped to their backs, forcing opponents to kill the creature before the werewolf kills them.<br /> <br /> It's easy, see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-09-2015, 03:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T13:10:06-07:00","id":585059,"title":"","content":"Adopting that for my game. Definitely gonna help with balance issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:56:00-07:00","id":585247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=584609#post584609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh-key. So, there isn't the only answer.<br /> I just don't know, should I like werewolves. 2.0. Their corebook is pretty solid for me, but... I can put up with they are weaker than Demons, Beasts and Mages (cuz this three spluts is elite of WoD-verse) and if they will be weaker than Mummy or Promethean, or even Geists and Changellings. But if they are weaker then vamps, for it make them misfits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this opinion based on experience, or pure speculation. Because I can say from personal experience, as someone whose run a lot of high action crossover, I've never had a Werewolf, PC or NPC, who couldn't pull their weight.<br /> <br /> If it is from experience consider that you may be running Werewolves outside their wheelhouse. Uratha will have a hard time showing up a Demon in the art of indirect espionage, or a Mage at plumbing the occult secrets of the astral world. But if it's being a savage hunter of things flesh and ephemera I can say with confidence Uratha are fucking terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:04:24-07:00","id":585384,"title":"","content":"even without Agg, Werewolves are just savage. just brutal monsters in combat. Take the Irakka build that attacks from stealth, you attack back, and he is reflexively gone. then rinses and repeats,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:59:05-07:00","id":585489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hackthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=585384#post585384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">even without Agg, Werewolves are just savage. just brutal monsters in combat. Take the Irakka build that attacks from stealth, you attack back, and he is reflexively gone. then rinses and repeats,</div> </div> </div> </div>This, with 8 again to Stealth rolls, including the one that completely negates your counter-attack, if there's even one, and Rote Action on an ungodly sneaking pool,which only get's bigger the more you fail to to notice him. All those 5 ghouls failed their perception? He's gonna take a +5 to the next one. And it'll keep stacking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T18:03:28-07:00","id":585493,"title":"","content":"8 again AND rote action...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T19:44:30-07:00","id":585543,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it isn't just the Rahu that can one shot an opponent this time around. I should finish rebuilding my old Irraka character, he had a shitload of XP (256) and PU 7 so I wonder how that would translate. I don't think I'd go that high in PU again, getting two stats to seven meant I had some underdeveloped skills and attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 07-09-2015, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T01:33:52-07:00","id":585765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hackthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=585493#post585493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8 again AND rote action...</div> </div> </div> </div>Boom! Staked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T05:10:47-07:00","id":585906,"title":"","content":"Its like I always say - its about playing to your strengths and the creativity of the players when it comes to crossover. If the wolf starts a'huntin', he's virtually unbeatable in his element. But when it comes to control, spy craft, being scary, or magical research, other games stand out as the better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T05:45:46-07:00","id":585931,"title":"","content":"Werewolves are pretty good at spying, actually. They just do it in a completely different manner to Demons. You can never be sure there isn't a werewolf standing in another plane of reality watching you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T23:37:58-07:00","id":586853,"title":"","content":"Interspecies Agencies. I'd do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T05:01:48-07:00","id":586982,"title":"","content":"Never said a wolf couldn't be good at it. Demons are just the best at it. Its their niche.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T14:08:14-07:00","id":588474,"title":"","content":"I think each would appreciate the ability of the other to get information that would be difficult for the other to obtain. Particularly Demons in this case, because when you don't respect the capabilities of possible opponents it often ends up in blown covers. I'm also sure they wouldn't mind the benefit of Lunacy helping to cover up their slip ups. To their point of view it would be like reality itself is working to reinforce werewolves' cover, without any special effort on the wolves' part. I also believe werewolves would appreciate the ability to go loud without risking losing control. Until I see what's in Beast I think Demon is the most crossover friendly of the lines, I can find easy hooks for them to interact with anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T14:23:54-07:00","id":588484,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't a werewolf be able to compensate for any lack in abilities by hunting down relevant spirits? There are spirits for every thing and concept and so forth. A werewolf could hunt down spirits of charisma and speaking and manipulation and presence and even spirits of vampires and become an incredibly majestic social being that gains essence for devouring blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T16:54:02-07:00","id":588582,"title":"","content":"I think vampires are like humans. There's no such thing as a vampire spirit for some bizarre reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T17:24:05-07:00","id":588611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=588582#post588582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think vampires are like humans. There's no such thing as a vampire spirit for some bizarre reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's called a Strix.<br /> <br /> I know, I know, Strix aren't actually spirits. But they're close, and they'd sure look like a vampire spirit to a werewolf. Or like some kind of weird owl host.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T18:03:00-07:00","id":588628,"title":"","content":"Even if there isn't Vampire the Requiem spirits, though I don't believe that, there's probably at least 'vampire' spirits, representing the concepts of vampires from horror movies, legends and other media that could be found.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T18:21:25-07:00","id":588671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=588628#post588628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if there isn't Vampire the Requiem spirits, though I don't believe that, there's probably at least 'vampire' spirits, representing the concepts of vampires from horror movies, legends and other media that could be found.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mosquito spirits and spirits of vampire bats are probably going to be less ridiculous to seek out, seeing as &quot;the spirit of a horror movie&quot; is more the demesne of goetia \u2014 most &quot;spirits of monsters&quot; are going to be conceptual spirits of fear and the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T18:27:20-07:00","id":588688,"title":"","content":"I think it would depend on how big into LARPing, legends and haunted places your setting is. Whether there's vampire tours in cities across the world and vampires are as big in media as they are in our world. Also whether you could track down an Elysium or other gathering of vampires.<br /> <br /> Between the fourth and tenth commandments I think at least some games would be able to incorporate them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 07-12-2015, 09:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T21:04:21-07:00","id":588823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=588688#post588688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it would depend on how big into LARPing, legends and haunted places your setting is.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem is more to do with the fact that &quot;vampirism&quot; is simultaneously poorly defined on a global level and more broad and complicated than can reasonably be assumed to arise from anything short of deliberate spiritual cultivation \u2014 a fear-spirit built from the terrors of exsanguination, deception, infection, and so on is probably going to resemble a vampire a fair bit and even draw imagery from it, but &quot;vampires&quot; are a little too involved to expect a focused flavor of resonance for.<br /> <br /> It's the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/40130-purified-and-the-god-machine-spirit-rules?p=209516#post209516\">spirits of destruction</a>&quot; issue from a different angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T21:18:51-07:00","id":588840,"title":"","content":"I could see werewolves approaching and dealing with strix however, they are basically vampire <br /> spirits...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T04:56:56-07:00","id":589032,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=588474#post588474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think each would appreciate the ability of the other to get information that would be difficult for the other to obtain.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, there's no information that a wolf can get that a demon couldn't get with the right power. Add in the paranoia and increased risk of Compromises that comes with working with the wolves, and its very unlikely that they'd work together. The more likely scenario is that the demon would feign being a wolf and use their powers to infiltrate the pack secretly.<br /> <br /> Lets not forget that not acting like a scared human when faced with werewolves is most likely acting out of character as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Particularly Demons in this case, because when you don't respect the capabilities of possible opponents it often ends up in blown covers. I'm also sure they wouldn't mind the benefit of Lunacy helping to cover up their slip ups. To their point of view it would be like reality itself is working to reinforce werewolves' cover, without any special effort on the wolves' part. I also believe werewolves would appreciate the ability to go loud without risking losing control. Until I see what's in Beast I think Demon is the most crossover friendly of the lines, I can find easy hooks for them to interact with anyone. </div> </div> </div> Demons are leery of everyone, because they never know when the God Machine is using someone. And Lunacy won't cover up their mistakes - Compromise checks happen irregardless if there's anyone to observe it.<br /> <br /> And, no, not only is Going Loud a very bad idea for a Demon (plus, lets not ignore that we have regular demon form or partial transformation!), but Demon Form does come with a series of Conditions that cause the demon in question to run out of control. Or start leaking aether. Or various other problems.<br /> <br /> Demon is a spy game for a reason. Doing this stuff carries a lot of risk for the Unchained with little pay out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=588484#post588484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't a werewolf be able to compensate for any lack in abilities by hunting down relevant spirits? There are spirits for every thing and concept and so forth. A werewolf could hunt down spirits of charisma and speaking and manipulation and presence and even spirits of vampires and become an incredibly majestic social being that gains essence for devouring blood.</div> </div> </div> </div> In theory, yes. Realistically, no. That requires leaving your territory to find these so-called relevant spirits, hunting them down, and forcing them to become your friend or into a fetish, and you need to feed them essence. The complications involved aren't easy to handwave away.<br /> <br /> I've seen people who've suggested that, in a wolf versus vampire fight, the werewolf could just call upon spirits of Helios to attack the vampires. That's only true if you ignore the logisitics of the issue here. 1) Helios spirits hate wolves, so convincing one takes effort. 2) you'd need to get them to do something out of character, and away from the source of their essence (ie at night). 3) you'd need a significant chimerage.<br /> <br /> Getting &quot;relevant&quot; spirits from outside your territory that you've not already established relationships with is not an easy thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=588628#post588628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if there isn't Vampire the Requiem spirits, though I don't believe that, there's probably at least 'vampire' spirits, representing the concepts of vampires from horror movies, legends and other media that could be found.</div> </div> </div> </div> In that case, we should have human spirits from the same movies. We don't really. We have movie spirits. Maybe even &quot;horror movie&quot; spirits, but I don't think that they would be even remotely close.<br /> <br /> Even if a &quot;vampire movie&quot; spirit existed, remember the predatorial nature of the Hisil, and the chances of one maintaining the ability to remain as a &quot;movie vampire&quot; when said movie isn't showing. Where would they get enough essence to feed without growing into something else?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=588611#post588611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's called a Strix.<br /> <br /> I know, I know, Strix aren't actually spirits. But they're close, and they'd sure look like a vampire spirit to a werewolf. Or like some kind of weird owl host.</div> </div> </div> </div> Would they look like a spirit? I mean, with how they're not in Twilight, and all. Definitely freaky, and likely to cause concern if it entered the wolf's territory, but none of their abilities would work on it, not even Death Gifts.<br /> <br /> I think calling it a spirit would be generous. Its less of one than a goetic or angel, since we're not even talking ephemeral beings here. There's less substance to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-13-2015, 08:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T05:24:26-07:00","id":589043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=589032#post589032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIn theory, yes. Realistically, no. That requires leaving your territory to find these so-called relevant spirits, hunting them down, and forcing them to become your friend or into a fetish, and you need to feed them essence. The complications involved aren't easy to handwave away.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's just about performing a Sacred Hunt rite and forcing it to give you a gift when you're done. Werewolves leave their territories all the time and there's always been nomadic ones. Even then, since vampires and werewolves are likely to share each other's territory you probably won't even have to leave it.<br /> <br /> Vampire bats are another thing, since they tend to be located in a single part of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've seen people who've suggested that, in a wolf versus vampire fight, the werewolf could just call upon spirits of Helios to attack the vampires. That's only true if you ignore the logisitics of the issue here. 1) Helios spirits hate wolves, so convincing one takes effort. 2) you'd need to get them to do something out of character, and away from the source of their essence (ie at night). 3) you'd need a significant chimerage.<br /> <br /> Getting &quot;relevant&quot; spirits from outside your territory that you've not already established relationships with is not an easy thing. </div> </div> </div>It's not an impossible thing, either. It's sort of what the game is about. That's why there's protectorates and lodges and entire organizations of werewolves searching the world to release another Firstborn to be their totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In that case, we should have human spirits from the same movies. We don't really. We have movie spirits. Maybe even &quot;horror movie&quot; spirits, but I don't think that they would be even remotely close.<br /> <br /> Even if a &quot;vampire movie&quot; spirit existed, remember the predatorial nature of the Hisil, and the chances of one maintaining the ability to remain as a &quot;movie vampire&quot; when said movie isn't showing. Where would they get enough essence to feed without growing into something else? </div> </div> </div>You seem down on a lot of ideas, that's fine. For your table. But there's no real reason to make up all these problems as if they wouldn't fit. Human spirits don't exist, that's about the only weird thing about the Shadow that's a fact.<br /> <br /> Where would they get enough essence? Simply find a vampire safe house, you even said they're likely to share one so you have multiple vampires in one place. Then you build a locus the way the book suggests. Or, alternatively, you use Resonance Shaping and make an existing locus into a vampire locus and let the spirits created by the reflections of the existing vampires to feed on it until they get strong.<br /> <br /> Satchel had a point with the horror movie angle but I'm sure it could still be overlooked by, say, a vampire movie marathon or one of the more vampire-oriented affairs, like the vampire tours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T05:31:13-07:00","id":589056,"title":"","content":"Why would you summon a Helion? A fire spirit would be much more co-operative. Reliable too, since sunlight does almost diddly squat against some vamps. <br /> <br /> On the flip side, it may well be that helions have an even bigger grudge against vampires than they do werewolves. Their material counterpart does tend to attempt to melt them on sight, after all. When it comes to the inheritors of an old grudge versus active abominations against nature, as they see them, I think they might agree to a temporary truce. The enemy of my enemy and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T05:41:49-07:00","id":589060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=589056#post589056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the flip side, it may well be that helions have an even bigger grudge against vampires than they do werewolves. Their material counterpart does tend to attempt to melt them on sight, after all. When it comes to the inheritors of an old grudge versus active abominations against nature, as they see them, I think they might agree to a temporary truce. The enemy of my enemy and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. And one of the sample fetishes in the second edition core book is a dawn shard, which improves the first impression Helions have to anyone who carries them. So presumably they aren't all kill-on-sight regarding werewolves anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T07:30:36-07:00","id":589170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's just about performing a Sacred Hunt rite and forcing it to give you a gift when you're done. Werewolves leave their territories all the time and there's always been nomadic ones. Even then, since vampires and werewolves are likely to share each other's territory you probably won't even have to leave it.<br /> <br /> Vampire bats are another thing, since they tend to be located in a single part of the world.</div> </div> </div> </div> Vampires do not create &quot;vampire spirits.&quot; They create spirits of blood, pain, lust, fear. Vampire bats are going to be spirits of creatures that feed on cows and insects - they're not afflicted by the vampire nature. Finding an equivalent to a vampire spirit is going to be HARD, if not impossible, for what you want. They're uncommon at the very least, and it'll require leaving any territory for a length of time is equivalent to abandoning it. And, while nomadic ones exist in theory, its immaterial when talking about PC packs. The overwhelming majority are going to be about their territory, since that is what the game is designed around.<br /> <br /> In general, this whole idea of &quot;all I have to do is find an appropriate spirit&quot; is nothing more than white room theorycraft, no different than trying to prove who's better in combat with a context-less void. Finding and supporting that spirit with appropriate essence is a major undertaking on its own if we're not talking about one of the more common choirs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=589043#post589043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You seem down on a lot of ideas, that's fine. For your table. But there's no real reason to make up all these problems as if they wouldn't fit. Human spirits don't exist, that's about the only weird thing about the Shadow that's a fact.</div> </div> </div> </div> Vampires fall under the same umbrella that humans do, you realize? Just as humans create various other spirits, so do vamps, with a tendency towards lust, blood, and pain spirits.<br /> <br /> Assuming the existence of other supernaturals as spirits is a departure from how the game is portrayed. Otherwise, there would be mage spirits running around, able to do anything a mage could, no? No, that's ridiculous.<br /> <br /> And the only thing I'm &quot;down on&quot; is the idea that a humanoid is suddenly appearing in the shadow, and with seemingly able to find any random spirit in casual reach. That's a bit of a stretch without completely undermining the entire way the Shadow ecology functions!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=589056#post589056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you summon a Helion? A fire spirit would be much more co-operative. Reliable too, since sunlight does almost diddly squat against some vamps.</div> </div> </div> </div> Because fire spirits are generally far weaker, or deeply asleep - who keeps major blazes active? You're lucky to find one, unless you go to a volcano or reactor, and even then, you'll be hard pressed to convince one to actually leave a major source of essence unless you can somehow provide a better alternative. Do you really want a powerful spirit who might look at your territory as kindling around?<br /> <br /> You're better off using moltovs and the fire elemental gift if you really wanted to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On the flip side, it may well be that helions have an even bigger grudge against vampires than they do werewolves. Their material counterpart does tend to attempt to melt them on sight, after all. When it comes to the inheritors of an old grudge versus active abominations against nature, as they see them, I think they might agree to a temporary truce. The enemy of my enemy and all that. </div> </div> </div> That's assuming that the helions have a grudge against vampires, and that they would assume vampires are abominations against nature - remember this isn't 1e, and no such prejudice exists by default. Rather large assumptions, in my opinion. Vampires, from a Hisil perspective, are no different than humans when it comes to creating essence. And spirits in the hisil are primarily concerned with essence above all, followed by spiritual duties in a number of cases.<br /> <br /> Vampires die in sunlight because, thematically, they're creatures of shadow and light is their bane. The Helions work to enforce a spiritual gravity in the Hisil and pushing everything down. There's nothing to suggest that opposites immediately hate each other. Do elk spirits see wolves as unholy abominations, because wolves eat them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=589060#post589060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. And one of the sample fetishes in the second edition core book is a dawn shard, which improves the first impression Helions have to anyone who carries them. So presumably they aren't all kill-on-sight regarding werewolves anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, the existance of the dawn shard actually implies that, while not kill-on-sight bad, impressions would still be generally poor. Why else would there be a need for such a thing if it wasn't bad?<br /> <br /> &quot;Ithaeur who\u2019ve dealt with Helions know all too well that Helios hasn\u2019t forgiven the Forsaken as his sister has. Mostly, it\u2019s because it\u2019s not in Helios\u2019 nature to change his mind about anything, but partly, it\u2019s because of the Sundering. Just as Luna gives the Hisil its ever-changing, reactive nature, Helios provides the impetus for spirits attempting to leave. By his nature, he forces everything away.&quot;<br /> <br /> This pretty much flat out states that sun-spirits don't like werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-13-2015, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T07:53:20-07:00","id":589184,"title":"","content":"Part of the sun's nature is to kill vampires. Ergo part of a helion's nature is to kill vampires. Maybe &quot;grudge&quot; is the wrong word. It's just what they do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T08:43:03-07:00","id":589250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=589170#post589170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Vampires do not create &quot;vampire spirits.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing this on? Are you quoting a book or just making it up?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And, while nomadic ones exist in theory, its immaterial when talking about PC packs. The overwhelming majority are going to be about their territory, since that is what the game is designed around. </div> </div> </div>The game is around the hunt, not staying in your territory and never leaving.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In general, this whole idea of &quot;all I have to do is find an appropriate spirit&quot; is nothing more than white room theorycraft, no different than trying to prove who's better in combat with a context-less void. Finding and supporting that spirit with appropriate essence is a major undertaking on its own if we're not talking about one of the more common choirs. </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry you feel that way. It's not about combat or trying to prove anyone as better. It's about theorizing what spirits of other supernaturals would be like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires fall under the same umbrella that humans do, you realize? Just as humans create various other spirits, so do vamps, with a tendency towards lust, blood, and pain spirits. </div> </div> </div>Can you give me a page number for this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assuming the existence of other supernaturals as spirits is a departure from how the game is portrayed. Otherwise, there would be mage spirits running around, able to do anything a mage could, no? No, that's ridiculous. </div> </div> </div>As Matt McFarland has pointed out, none of the games have been built for crossover beyond stereotypes and minor interactions. While I doubt there's mage spirits, I'm sure there are magic spirits, spirits of the occult, and in first edition we had spirits of the Witch's Moon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the only thing I'm &quot;down on&quot; is the idea that a humanoid is suddenly appearing in the shadow, and with seemingly able to find any random spirit in casual reach. That's a bit of a stretch without completely undermining the entire way the Shadow ecology functions! </div> </div> </div>Do you have a problem with the Shadow Twin Tell, too?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because fire spirits are generally far weaker, or deeply asleep - who keeps major blazes active? You're lucky to find one, unless you go to a volcano or reactor, and even then, you'll be hard pressed to convince one to actually leave a major source of essence unless you can somehow provide a better alternative. Do you really want a powerful spirit who might look at your territory as kindling around? </div> </div> </div>Predators explains that fire elementals hide to blend in, but there's nothing to suggest they're 'far weaker' or 'deeply asleep.' Where are you getting that? Also, all it requires is a memory. A fire having destroyed a building ten years ago can leave fire spirits burning strongly now. The Chicago book had the city ravaged by vestiges of the Chicago fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, the existance of the dawn shard actually implies that, while not kill-on-sight bad, impressions would still be generally poor. Why else would there be a need for such a thing if it wasn't bad?<br /> <br /> &quot;Ithaeur who\u2019ve dealt with Helions know all too well that Helios hasn\u2019t forgiven the Forsaken as his sister has. Mostly, it\u2019s because it\u2019s not in Helios\u2019 nature to change his mind about anything, but partly, it\u2019s because of the Sundering. Just as Luna gives the Hisil its ever-changing, reactive nature, Helios provides the impetus for spirits attempting to leave. By his nature, he forces everything away.&quot;<br /> <br /> This pretty much flat out states that sun-spirits don't like werewolves. </div> </div> </div>'Helios has never forgiven the People for his sibling\u2019s lover\u2019s death, and his Helions range from disdainful to hostile to werewolves.'<br /> <br /> They're not all hostile. They may not like them, but that can clearly be worked through.<br /> <br /> We get it, you don't like it. Are you going to add anything to the conversation than trying to tell people what they can't do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T09:12:28-07:00","id":589286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=589170#post589170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Assuming the existence of other supernaturals as spirits is a departure from how the game is portrayed. Otherwise, there would be mage spirits running around, able to do anything a mage could, no? No, that's ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost Mages are close enough.<br /> <br /> Besides, who needs a Helion's consent to bind it into a flash-bang grenade to make one of Blade 2's sunlight grenades, hmm?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T09:44:48-07:00","id":589327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Actually, the existance of the dawn shard actually implies that, while not kill-on-sight bad, impressions would still be generally poor. Why else would there be a need for such a thing if it wasn't bad? </div> </div> </div>Actually, Most Spirits have poor/bad impressions of werewolves, no? The fact that a fetish exists means only that someone thought to create something to improve relations with a specific spirit court. And that is all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T09:45:25-07:00","id":589328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=589032#post589032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWould they look like a spirit? I mean, with how they're not in Twilight, and all. Definitely freaky, and likely to cause concern if it entered the wolf's territory, but none of their abilities would work on it, not even Death Gifts.<br /> <br /> I think calling it a spirit would be generous. Its less of one than a goetic or angel, since we're not even talking ephemeral beings here. There's less substance to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the werewolves of Tokyo sure seem to think they look like spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T10:15:36-07:00","id":589344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=589328#post589328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the werewolves of Tokyo sure seem to think they look like spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the readers sure seem to think the Tengu look like Strix. There's an important distinction built into the order of events here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:12:16-07:00","id":589380,"title":"","content":"There's similarities, but the eye color difference has always stood out to me. If only because the yellow eyes thing has always seemed like the sole true identifier of the strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T06:13:14-07:00","id":590169,"title":"","content":"The Tengu/Strix thing is, to me, just a red herring that the storyteller can make real or not. Are they Strix? Are they something else? YOU DECIDE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T08:58:53-07:00","id":590248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=590169#post590169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tengu/Strix thing is, to me, just a red herring that the storyteller can make real or not. Are they Strix? Are they something else? YOU DECIDE.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the impression I got as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T22:09:10-07:00","id":590884,"title":"","content":"Or the Tengu and Strix are roughly analogous to Forsaken and Pure. Different members of the same family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T22:38:17-07:00","id":590898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=590884#post590884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the Tengu and Strix are roughly analogous to Forsaken and Pure. Different members of the same family.</div> </div> </div> </div>The key problem with this is that the Strix are like the Kindred in that the term exists as an umbrella for a bunch of similar creatures that have gotten more similar over time through mutual assembly and consumption, whereas the Tengu are a type of supernatural being that resemble shadowy birds, possess corpses and vampires, and are thought by werewolves to be a class of spirit.<br /> <br /> None of the latter qualities are particularly uncommon in the supernatural world and both the eye color and the agenda are off-model for the Strix, to say nothing of how the Three and Four Diamonds writeup makes no actual mention of any peculiarities of behavior among the Tokyo Strix and Beast's writeup for Tokyo corroborates the Uratha's assessment of the Tengu's nature.<br /> <br /> If I had to draw an analogy, it'd be more to do with the relationship between the Principle and the God-Machine \u2014 two vaguely similar aesthetics on two similarly mysterious factions with conspicuous differences in behavior and methodology, whereby there is sufficient grounds to either suggest an ontological link between the two or reject such a connection as suits any given game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T19:13:47-07:00","id":593463,"title":"","content":"Actually, werewolves can solve a lot of problems using spirits. But it requirers long preparation and strategic development of relations between pack and local spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T01:46:49-07:00","id":593635,"title":"","content":"Personally I can't think of anything more boring to me, when it comes to creating a horror setting, than trying to twink out a combat monster of any game line. After the CWoD I'm glad aggravated damage is rare. It makes it more memorable and makes dealing it actually mean more than CWoD's comparative plethora of agg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T03:38:40-07:00","id":593683,"title":"","content":"The thing is, Horror stories aren't actually all that scary for the monster, usually. So WoD can easily fall into the trap where the setting is absolutely terrifying, but only for the NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T10:34:40-07:00","id":593974,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Butchering the mooks of your local drug enterprise with Down and Dirty isn't much difficult, or scary.<br /> <br /> The problem is when you suddenly feel like pulling that out in your office/family home/mall (pesky spirit influences).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T10:44:51-07:00","id":593981,"title":"","content":"Or when you realize they're part of a larger operation that has ties to the supernatural and once someone realizes it wasn't a human that splattered Nickle Tony across the room they'll reach out to their more shadowy allies.<br /> <br /> Even if they haven't put together the supernatural bit, they may decide to send a message if they find evidence of who's doing it, through friends and family, which to a werewolf is likely their pack.<br /> <br /> We're sort of in that situation now. It's not particularly scary just offing some guy, but the pack's had a lot to dwell on it between what it means to do that so easily and what the repercussions of it are going to be, and whether or not we'll be able to survive it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T10:54:49-07:00","id":593990,"title":"","content":"I think that's where the personal horror comes in. Vanilla WoD is there for your external horror, where you're afraid of the monsters that are out there. The monster splats are internal horror, where you're afraid of the monster you've become. That's why I'm a big fan of the Putting It On The Line rules, they really up the &quot;dear god, what have I done?&quot; factor that makes being a werewolf scary. Even without that though, there's a sort of meta-horror in taking a step back and realizing how far gone your character is, that she can murder people and eat them because she was feeling a bit too human and needed to bounce back towards spirit, as if that's totally normal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T10:55:19-07:00","id":593991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=593683#post593683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, Horror stories aren't actually all that scary for the monster, usually. So WoD can easily fall into the trap where the setting is absolutely terrifying, but only for the NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, there are a lot of types of horror. Some types of horror are facilitated by some mechanics, others by different mechanics or setting themes or tones. I mean it's almost like we have different game lines for different types of horror...<br /> <br /> Though I confess as of yet I don't know which type of horror involves comparing splat e-peens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T11:04:02-07:00","id":594010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=593991#post593991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I confess as of yet I don't know which type of horror involves comparing splat e-peens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. While impotence in the face of a more powerful force is sort of a staple in horror, 'balance' as an issue is more of an OOC, game concern that has no bearing on it. But to be fair Lashet never said they were concerned about the horror aspect of the game, just how they perceived werewolves as weaker than others and that made them undesirable to play.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T16:04:32-07:00","id":619531,"title":"","content":"Aggravated damage is rare from Gifts and other powers for all supernatural creatures and for good reasons. But there are no problem to bring aggravated damage potential to any prepared fight and I see no issue with that.<br /> <br /> I also hate any discussion with even trying to compare two combatants when removing the narrative or any environment that can effect the outcome of an encounter.<br /> <br /> I also strongly dislike any discussion where one dimensional total fictional characters with totally ridiculous stats are discussed. To get back to Werewolf versus Vampire fight for one thing.<br /> <br /> I would say that given the same amount of experience most Werewolves would prevail over a Vampire in a sudden and violent situational confrontation. But if you put it into a narrative story I would say its more about the intent and conviction by either party and which medium they use to try and destroy the other and for what reason they do so.<br /> <br /> When it comes to Vampires versus Werewolves in general there are very large gaps in experience between a young wolf and an old vampire. You can't really compare a 150 year old vampire with a 35 year old Werewolf when it comes to general power and influence... even if said Werewolf would kill that vampire in single combat in the blink of an eye. Would that Werewolf be able to bypass all the combined powers the vampire possess unless this is a random brawl on the street?<br /> <br /> A pack of young and passionate Werewolves might feel invincible on paper but they really are not, they still have limited experience, knowledge and influences in order to deal with a vast majority of really old nasties out there. Sure... they can beat pretty much anything in single combat at their own terms... but will it always be like that in reality though?<br /> <br /> Most Vampires for example will not be direct combat monsters and even those that are will eventually revert to less combative demeanor as they age, purely as a survival mechanism. That is what it takes for a vampire to survive in the long run.<br /> <br /> I believe this is mostly true for &quot;real&quot; Werewolves as well. Young Werewolves might be bad asses with high physical attributes and appropriate gifts and merits. But as they age they will tend to rely more on mental and social attributes and skills rather than brute force... they will also see their physical prowess to start waning as well... I do guess that Werewoves need to keep training physical strength in order to keep it in the same way a regular human need to, which is why you will not see Werewolves with 5 in all physical attributes that often (if ever)... and the ones that have will only be able to retain them for a short brief time anyway. This is speaking from a narrative point of view.<br /> <br /> How much experience must not these supreme combat monsters have acquired and how do they survive that long without much competence in other areas?<br /> There will always be someone stronger and/or just luckier or plain smarter than them to beat them in their rather violent life. In order to attain these ridiculous power levels in combat you will have to survive a ridiculous amount of life and death situations. How likely are such characters to exist, especially for a Werewolf with such limited time span before they get old and weak?<br /> Remember that it usually takes a failure to gain much experience (for the most part) and it should be harder and harder to fail as you grow in power. I can also see that the possible disastrous effect of failure should be higher the tougher you actually are since the forces opposing you need to more and more lethal.<br /> <br /> And then... who is so brainless as they plan to fight anyone at anything resembling equal terms?<br /> What creature would go on the offensive if ambushed not knowing what the nature of the ambush or the trap is?<br /> Anyone who lived long enough and managed to get the experience needed to get this far would flee and fight another day during such encounters. The same is true for a failed ambush if you encounter some tough or unexpected problems.<br /> <br /> Single combat between two entities, especially between different supernatural beings should be extremely rare. Perhaps if there is a personal vendetta between two creatures with a similar type of notion, such as the way of the warrior and honor perhaps?<br /> <br /> Anyway... just because one system have the &quot;potential&quot; of producing the more perfect warrior does not mean it is realistic to find such a character in a game outside of meta-gaming or pure number crunching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T03:06:19-07:00","id":619898,"title":"","content":"In 2nd ed I don' t know if is there any reference for werewolve' s aging, not in the main book, but in first ed you can find many references of really old werewolves who didn't wan at all with aging, but the opossite.<br /> Also remember the game states a max atribute skill cap of 10 so I would say high PU werewolves are virtually inmortal but as their lives are far more violent, there aren' t many ancient werewolves. But those who manage to live through centuries of hunt should be really though and smart badasses. Just look at Red Stick from war against the pure, and he's '' only '' 200 years old...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7208-beltrajor","name":"beltrajor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T04:40:55-07:00","id":619917,"title":"","content":"If anything it makes <i>more</i> sense for werewolves to live longer and longer as their primal urge goes up in 2e than it did before. Now it increases how fast they regenerate, which is generally assumed to be the reason they don't tend to die of natural causes in the first place. Which also means that any that <i>get</i> that old are most certainly not to be fucked with.<br /> <br /> Basically you need to think of elder werewolves as Cohen the Barbarian from Discworld, only even older, still in their prime and a hell of a lot more dangerous in a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T11:33:59-07:00","id":620341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beltrajor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=619898#post619898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2nd ed I don' t know if is there any reference for werewolve' s aging, not in the main book, but in first ed you can find many references of really old werewolves who didn't wan at all with aging, but the opossite.<br /> Also remember the game states a max atribute skill cap of 10 so I would say high PU werewolves are virtually inmortal but as their lives are far more violent, there aren' t many ancient werewolves. But those who manage to live through centuries of hunt should be really though and smart badasses. Just look at Red Stick from war against the pure, and he's '' only '' 200 years old...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's worth noting that all of those references to old wolves all occur in supplement books. The reason 2e doesn't have any references to werewolf aging is because it quite frankly doesn't have that stuff <i>yet.</i> Objectively, it makes little sense to compare a book with several in terms of content and fluff.<br /> <br /> But as Elfive states, with constantly ramping up regeneration, werewolves who reach that old probably don't suffer the same delibitating effects of old age due to simply breaking the Hayflick limit. They never stop regenerating and replacing damage, even old wounds from PreChange life start fading away as new limbs and crippling injuries are healed over. The rules pretty much state how extreme werewolf regeneration is.<br /> <br /> In fact, because of this, I almost think that it's actually conceivable for a hundred year old werewolf to look <i>younger</i> than his thirty year old <i>grandkids. </i>Or for changed Seniors to start taking up athletics and progressively seem to appear younger, more in their prime as their bodies start repairing damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:06:49-07:00","id":620609,"title":"","content":"I would agree that Werewolves probably will outlive their human cousins but there might still be a problem with DNA degradation despite regeneration. The regeneration power might work of previous DNA and if that has changed so does the regeneration power.<br /> <br /> Unless the book or rules states otherwise I do think we have to assume they age more normal than not in my opinion even if they can live longer. It there are the odd Wolf that manage to cheat death for a long time due to unnatural causes that may be so. But if it is a general rule there should be some information about it and not just speculations?<br /> <br /> Perhaps someone can enlighten us as to the immortality of Werewolves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:17:27-07:00","id":620622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JorgenCAB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=620609#post620609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless the book or rules states otherwise I do think we have to assume they age more normal than not in my opinion even if they can live longer.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's fiction on the books that includes a werewolf making it known that, contrary to what her appearance indicates and her fake driver's license says, she's seventy-odd years old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:23:33-07:00","id":620633,"title":"","content":"For the record, said story is in Blood of the Wolf right before they explain that, at the very least, a werewolf would be able to live up to twice the lifespan of a human, maybe more. No one knows since they keep getting killed before old age ever shows up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:31:18-07:00","id":620637,"title":"","content":"It was mostly expressed in first edition through powerful npcs. To my knowledge there was only one Primal Urge 10 werewolf ever written of, an Irraka in Signs of the Moon. He was just over 400 years old, and didn't look it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:34:55-07:00","id":620642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JorgenCAB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=620609#post620609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps someone can enlighten us as to the immortality of Werewolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves are half-spirit, spirits are effectively immortal. Have a spiritual side more developed than your own flesh side (PU 6+) and you're effectively immortal.<br /> <br /> Examples include but aren't limited to: Red Sticks, The Wolf in the Woods, Voice of Shadow, Blake The-Mad-Doctor Calloway, Wandering Voice, Aisling Tulane and Edward Shattersong K'ruuk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:49:22-07:00","id":620658,"title":"","content":"So... you can sum it up with that Werewolves can live long lives and probably live about twice that of humans in general but some very powerful ones are basically turned into spirits and live forever.<br /> <br /> So, you will have Werewolves that live roughly as long as humans up until immortality with about double that of Humans as the most common. That seem reasonable to me...<br /> <br /> At least the body dies even if the Spirit somehow perhaps can survive and be reborn in a new body perhaps, I'm not too versed in Werewolf mythology?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:54:31-07:00","id":620667,"title":"","content":"You can end up a spirit for certain if you die whilst using certain gifts and rituals. Outside of that it's up in the air. There <i>are</i> things called ancestor spirits but these are generally not thought to be literal ancestors. Maybe they are though. Who knows? <br /> <br /> I always thought the notion of a particularly legendary werewolf living on as a lune of their auspice was a cool idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T16:55:25-07:00","id":620715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=620667#post620667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can end up a spirit for certain if you die whilst using certain gifts and rituals. Outside of that it's up in the air. There <i>are</i> things called ancestor spirits but these are generally not thought to be literal ancestors. Maybe they are though. Who knows?<br /> <br /> I always thought the notion of a particularly legendary werewolf living on as a lune of their auspice was a cool idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's possible, a mighty Lune have shred at least one Hunter in Darkness flesh which was reborn as a spirit, which would then take it's place as a lodge patron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T17:47:03-07:00","id":620756,"title":"","content":"The only real rule offering immortality as far as I know is through the Maleadar for the Bale Hounds, where they do become an avatar of the Maeljin they serve.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, rules as written, like has been said they live twice as normal as a regular human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T23:43:57-07:00","id":620949,"title":"","content":"Time and future publishings will tell, but I would say that once a werewolf reaches so high PU (7+or so..) that he can only feed from spirits, it's spirit half has become so prevalent that should be functionally inmortal. for now, I' ll just adhere to existing fluff ( not that there are such drastical changes that make all existing lore worthless ( as opposed to whot happened with wwta)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7208-beltrajor","name":"beltrajor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T23:57:25-07:00","id":620954,"title":"","content":"Of course, harmony is also a measure of how human or spirity a werewolf is now, so if you wanted to you could say that werewolves just stop ageing whenever their Primal Urge exceeds it. It means you can get the standard bodhisattva werewolf but also poor, ban-ridden sods who just forgot how to mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T04:40:03-07:00","id":621081,"title":"","content":"Well, there's Lycaon-Ur as a possible example in 2e.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T05:06:31-07:00","id":621090,"title":"","content":"If what he says is true, he's lived for many centuries. But i find him quite dissapointing for such an ancient werewolf despite him having many gifts. I somewhat expect MORE from an ancient monster that serves as herald of a powerfull idigam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7208-beltrajor","name":"beltrajor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T05:32:24-07:00","id":621110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>beltrajor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/566515-aggravated-damage?p=621090#post621090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If what he says is true, he's lived for many centuries. But i find him quite dissapointing for such an ancient werewolf despite him having many gifts. I somewhat expect MORE from an ancient monster that serves as herald of a powerfull idigam.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, there's also the Penitent in 2e - who is the one you're thinking of, the herald of the Deceiver Lune. He's Primal Urge 7.<br /> <br /> Lycaon-Ur is a different entity, in the Field of Dogs hunting ground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T09:08:00-07:00","id":621370,"title":"","content":"In first edition the only werewolf I can think of with immortality, or at least 'unending youth and vigor,' was Olivia Citysmith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:19:47-07:00","id":626658,"title":"","content":"Actualy, I did some &quot;white room&quot; fight. Vamp with agravated claws vs Wer with Hit-and-Run, which were created for the same exp. It was long fight (both of them debunked each other's attacks untill cometly spend their Blood/Essence pools) but then werewolf kill vampire for three turns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:46:22-07:00","id":626987,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't a tonge of fire 5 werewolf clear an entire &quot; white room&quot; worth of vampires? The mechanics for influences are quite vague, but mass create + strenghten sounds pretty good to me...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7208-beltrajor","name":"beltrajor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:55:26-07:00","id":626993,"title":"","content":"Throw some Catastrophe in there and you can clear an entire territory of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T14:58:37-07:00","id":626996,"title":"","content